1
00:00:01,268 --> 00:00:06,672
(Their first morning in Bangkok)

2
00:00:07,241 --> 00:00:10,410
(They planned to leave at 7:00 a.m.)

3
00:00:11,078 --> 00:00:13,846
(Won Ji and Gabee's room)

4
00:00:14,314 --> 00:00:16,916
(Won Ji is already up.)

5
00:00:18,819 --> 00:00:19,619
(The alarm goes off.)

6
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,788
(Glancing over)

7
00:00:22,422 --> 00:00:24,156
Did you sleep well?

8
00:00:24,157 --> 00:00:25,190
Good morning.

9
00:00:26,226 --> 00:00:27,426
Did I snore?

10
00:00:27,728 --> 00:00:29,262
- No.
- Good.

11
00:00:30,631 --> 00:00:31,998
What time did you get up?

12
00:00:31,999 --> 00:00:35,034
- I woke up at 5:30.
- What?

13
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:36,703
So I took a shower.

14
00:00:37,938 --> 00:00:40,406
(Gabee heads out to shower too.)

15
00:00:41,108 --> 00:00:43,609
(Meanwhile, in the younger members' room)

16
00:00:44,912 --> 00:00:47,914
(They're still fast asleep.)

17
00:00:48,649 --> 00:00:52,185
(Sian fell asleep in the exact same spot.)

18
00:00:52,953 --> 00:00:56,289
(Sprawled out)

19
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,359
(Sleeping in completely
different positions)

20
00:01:00,661 --> 00:01:02,228
Don't we need to pack again today?

21
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:03,129
Right.

22
00:01:03,864 --> 00:01:04,531
(Today's mission)

23
00:01:04,556 --> 00:01:07,300
(Fill the suitcase with valuable items
as you travel.)

24
00:01:07,402 --> 00:01:08,468
This is all my stuff.

25
00:01:08,469 --> 00:01:09,769
- I don't have much.
- Me neither.

26
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:11,337
I only have three bags.

27
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,905
Same here!

28
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:16,242
It's not really an issue, though.

29
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:18,410
Because if I'm missing something...

30
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:19,878
Yeah. We can just share.

31
00:01:20,214 --> 00:01:22,015
- That's nice.
- It's not so bad.

32
00:01:24,085 --> 00:01:25,718
My makeup is going to melt off anyway.

33
00:01:25,719 --> 00:01:26,986
That's true.

34
00:01:26,987 --> 00:01:29,489
No point in putting in too much effort
if it's just going to melt.

35
00:01:30,324 --> 00:01:31,324
Right.

36
00:01:34,861 --> 00:01:38,497
(Carefully)

37
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:40,534
Why aren't they up yet?

38
00:01:41,568 --> 00:01:43,769
I'm sure they know we're leaving at seven.

39
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:45,137
Right.

40
00:01:45,906 --> 00:01:47,306
What are they doing?

41
00:01:47,307 --> 00:01:48,841
(Current time: 6:45 a.m.)

42
00:01:49,409 --> 00:01:50,676
Do you want to try this?

43
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:54,079
Just wearing this
makes me feel so put together.

44
00:01:54,548 --> 00:01:56,616
- Want me to try it?
- I'll let you use it.

45
00:01:56,617 --> 00:01:58,852
I'll put this on before we go upstairs.

46
00:01:59,486 --> 00:02:00,519
Should we pretend to be mad?

47
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,054
Yeah, let's do it.

48
00:02:02,557 --> 00:02:04,591
- What if we say, "You rude little brats?"
- Great.

49
00:02:05,058 --> 00:02:07,426
(Immediate reaction)

50
00:02:08,522 --> 00:02:09,727
Let's try that.

51
00:02:09,728 --> 00:02:11,431
I've always wanted to try
something like that.

52
00:02:11,741 --> 00:02:12,808
Let's pretend to be mean.

53
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:14,501
Like in the boot camp.

54
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:15,401
Okay.

55
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:16,702
Let me do it then.

56
00:02:16,703 --> 00:02:17,869
I need you to say it with me, though.

57
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:20,139
- Me?
- You have to say it too.

58
00:02:20,574 --> 00:02:21,440
Okay.

59
00:02:21,742 --> 00:02:23,525
I'll stand right behind you
with my arms crossed.

60
00:02:23,549 --> 00:02:25,478
- You're so cute.
- I'll cross my arms.

61
00:02:26,547 --> 00:02:28,647
I feel like I'd look cool wearing this.

62
00:02:30,784 --> 00:02:33,552
You don't look scary with that on at all.

63
00:02:33,553 --> 00:02:35,522
My lips are going to be so red, though.

64
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:39,191
By the way, they actually are late.

65
00:02:39,694 --> 00:02:41,961
So we can't just end it
with "Hey, just kidding!" and a smile.

66
00:02:42,495 --> 00:02:44,030
- That'd be awkward.
- Yes.

67
00:02:44,398 --> 00:02:45,099
(Snorting)

68
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,768
Let's go get them...

69
00:02:48,236 --> 00:02:49,302
right after I put this on.

70
00:02:49,537 --> 00:02:50,403
Okay.

71
00:02:50,804 --> 00:02:51,905
Let me go teach them a lesson.

72
00:02:52,139 --> 00:02:53,039
Let's set them straight.

73
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:53,940
(Her features stand out even more.)

74
00:02:54,374 --> 00:02:55,474
It's 6:53 a.m. now.

75
00:02:55,475 --> 00:02:57,509
(Girls, here we come.)

76
00:02:58,178 --> 00:03:00,956
(The older girls are on their way.)

77
00:03:00,981 --> 00:03:01,781
Right?

78
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:03,949
- By the way,
- Yeah?

79
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:05,551
how are you going to set them straight?

80
00:03:06,286 --> 00:03:07,154
We walk in...

81
00:03:08,088 --> 00:03:09,722
and say, "You lazy girls!"

82
00:03:09,723 --> 00:03:11,323
(I like that.)

83
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:12,725
"You lazy girls!"

84
00:03:12,726 --> 00:03:13,626
(The sun is already up!)

85
00:03:13,627 --> 00:03:14,761
"You lazy girls!"

86
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:17,497
Let's burst through the door.

87
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,701
(One second before setting them straight)

88
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:25,170
You lazy girls, what are you doing?

89
00:03:25,171 --> 00:03:26,940
That didn't sound mean at all.

90
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,440
We're ready.

91
00:03:28,842 --> 00:03:30,208
You should go get changed.

92
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,744
It's 6:53 a.m.

93
00:03:31,745 --> 00:03:33,279
The taxi is coming at 7:00.

94
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,613
You lazy...

95
00:03:35,115 --> 00:03:36,249
We were going to set you guys straight.

96
00:03:36,274 --> 00:03:37,117
What is up with your lips?

97
00:03:37,218 --> 00:03:38,451
(It ended up making them laugh instead.)

98
00:03:38,452 --> 00:03:40,287
- I borrowed it.
- She used mine.

99
00:03:41,588 --> 00:03:43,022
Girls, we're in a hurry.

100
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:45,224
- We're late.
- In five minutes...

101
00:03:45,526 --> 00:03:46,825
The taxi is arriving in five minutes,

102
00:03:46,826 --> 00:03:48,762
- but we haven't even packed.
- Right. What time is it now?

103
00:03:49,696 --> 00:03:50,763
Hurry up!

104
00:03:50,764 --> 00:03:52,998
We have to pack downstairs,
so bring your things down.

105
00:03:52,999 --> 00:03:54,266
Bring your things downstairs.

106
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:55,100
- Okay.
- Okay.

107
00:03:55,504 --> 00:03:57,203
Gabee, that was cool.

108
00:03:58,005 --> 00:03:58,905
Gabee.

109
00:03:59,139 --> 00:03:59,972
That was...

110
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:01,641
quiet, but charismatic.

111
00:04:01,909 --> 00:04:03,242
Soft charisma.

112
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,243
It wasn't that.

113
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,046
Why don't we start packing first?

114
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,748
Right. Let's claim our spots first.

115
00:04:10,817 --> 00:04:13,685
(The older girls start packing first.)

116
00:04:13,686 --> 00:04:14,587
Here they come.

117
00:04:14,822 --> 00:04:16,322
You came down fast.

118
00:04:17,224 --> 00:04:18,090
Nice.

119
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:19,058
(Harimu joins them.)

120
00:04:19,059 --> 00:04:19,992
Come on.

121
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:23,328
What is this? Clothes? Come on.

122
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,097
There you are.

123
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:27,132
Looks good. You don't have much.

124
00:04:27,133 --> 00:04:28,467
I only have this.

125
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:30,970
Oh, really?

126
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:33,405
We already trimmed things down earlier.

127
00:04:33,406 --> 00:04:35,275
Right. That definitely helped.

128
00:04:36,076 --> 00:04:37,243
I should go grab it.

129
00:04:37,244 --> 00:04:38,944
It's in the bathroom.

130
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:40,280
Why did we lay them out like this?

131
00:04:40,305 --> 00:04:41,357
(Closing the suitcase)

132
00:04:43,917 --> 00:04:46,118
We could pack more if we wanted to,

133
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:48,387
but we need room for laundry and stuff.

134
00:04:48,755 --> 00:04:50,208
Want me to overline your lips for you?

135
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:51,790
- Sure.
- Your hair...

136
00:04:53,026 --> 00:04:54,059
Is this okay?

137
00:04:54,395 --> 00:04:56,295
She did such a good job
overlining your lips.

138
00:04:56,319 --> 00:04:57,296
You look amazing.

139
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:58,597
It looks so good on you.

140
00:04:59,232 --> 00:05:00,966
I love it.

141
00:05:01,201 --> 00:05:02,401
- That's nice.
- Looks great.

142
00:05:02,402 --> 00:05:04,136
- You look like a bird.
- You look like Betty Boop.

143
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,505
- Betty Boop.
- It suits you.

144
00:05:06,773 --> 00:05:07,673
Betty Boop.

145
00:05:08,175 --> 00:05:09,242
(Expressing her gratitude
with a dramatic performance)

146
00:05:09,243 --> 00:05:10,610
She's transforming.

147
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:11,977
She's transforming!

148
00:05:12,546 --> 00:05:13,880
- She really is!
- She's transforming.

149
00:05:14,114 --> 00:05:17,583
I'm transforming from an Australopithecus
into an "it girl."

150
00:05:18,518 --> 00:05:20,652
- An "it girl"?
- Transforming into an "it girl."

151
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:21,587
This is fun.

152
00:05:21,588 --> 00:05:22,955
(Those lips turned her into an "it girl.")

153
00:05:23,090 --> 00:05:25,058
- Hye Rim, did you put on sunscreen?
- No, not yet.

154
00:05:25,059 --> 00:05:27,193
Put some on. Let's do it together.

155
00:05:27,427 --> 00:05:28,962
Who hasn't put on sunscreen yet?

156
00:05:28,963 --> 00:05:30,629
Let me put some here.

157
00:05:30,630 --> 00:05:31,698
Want some?

158
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:34,166
Oh, dear.

159
00:05:35,235 --> 00:05:37,436
It feels like a serum.

160
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:39,371
(Slathering on more sunscreen)

161
00:05:39,372 --> 00:05:41,942
The tops of my feet
got so sunburned yesterday.

162
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:43,275
- Really?
- Really?

163
00:05:43,276 --> 00:05:44,444
They got so dark.

164
00:05:44,445 --> 00:05:46,112
The sun here must be super strong.

165
00:05:46,439 --> 00:05:48,440
We might finish this whole thing soon.

166
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:50,984
We might use it all up
while we're in Thailand.

167
00:05:51,585 --> 00:05:53,519
- Are we good to go?
- Let's go.

168
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,121
Good morning, everyone.

169
00:05:55,122 --> 00:05:57,390
- Here's today's travel budget.
- What's that?

170
00:05:57,391 --> 00:05:59,392
(Reaching out)

171
00:05:59,593 --> 00:06:02,862
That's my brush.
Why are you using it like that?

172
00:06:03,865 --> 00:06:06,132
Her brush has a whole new purpose now.

173
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,834
Our treasurer.

174
00:06:07,835 --> 00:06:10,569
Let me double-check
if the amount is right.

175
00:06:10,770 --> 00:06:14,039
Wait, what? It feels like less.

176
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,542
Today's accommodation cost...

177
00:06:15,615 --> 00:06:16,981
- plus yesterday's taxi rental fee.
- Did you take that out?

178
00:06:17,044 --> 00:06:18,078
Excluding that.

179
00:06:18,079 --> 00:06:19,212
- They deducted it.
- That's fine then.

180
00:06:19,213 --> 00:06:20,179
Let's put in 1,000 baht each.

181
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:21,647
(They only received 8,000 baht.)

182
00:06:21,648 --> 00:06:23,249
Let's go now.

183
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:24,117
To the taxi driver.

184
00:06:24,585 --> 00:06:27,186
Okay. Let's go!

185
00:06:27,287 --> 00:06:28,220
Okay.

186
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:30,088
It's heavy.

187
00:06:30,089 --> 00:06:33,692
- Good morning.
- Good morning, world.

188
00:06:34,127 --> 00:06:35,295
Is that our taxi?

189
00:06:35,962 --> 00:06:37,296
- It's huge.
- It's huge!

190
00:06:37,297 --> 00:06:39,932
- So much bigger than yesterday's.
- I was so squished yesterday.

191
00:06:40,468 --> 00:06:42,234
It's on a whole different level.

192
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:44,336
- Hello.
- Hello.

193
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:47,039
Having just one suitcase is so convenient.

194
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,174
Traveling light is the way to go.

195
00:06:49,943 --> 00:06:51,077
Oh, my goodness!

196
00:06:52,512 --> 00:06:53,812
This car is so nice.

197
00:06:54,281 --> 00:06:55,982
(Harimu, the youngest, sits in the back.)

198
00:06:55,996 --> 00:06:56,962
Okay.

199
00:06:57,117 --> 00:06:58,384
- Nice.
- This is great.

200
00:06:58,385 --> 00:06:59,351
I love it.

201
00:06:59,755 --> 00:07:01,654
- Okay, let's go.
- Let's go!

202
00:07:01,655 --> 00:07:03,923
Everyone, buckle up.

203
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:05,691
So nice.

204
00:07:06,126 --> 00:07:07,460
- Day 2!
- Day 2!

205
00:07:09,095 --> 00:07:11,927
(On their way to the floating market)

206
00:07:11,952 --> 00:07:14,354
(An 1 hour and 40 minutes
driving distance)

207
00:07:14,668 --> 00:07:16,435
What's your name?

208
00:07:18,471 --> 00:07:20,338
- My name is Tony.
- Tony!

209
00:07:20,574 --> 00:07:21,541
Tony Stark.

210
00:07:21,775 --> 00:07:22,775
Hi.

211
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:24,744
(Iron Man?)

212
00:07:24,745 --> 00:07:25,744
(You're embarrassing us.)

213
00:07:25,745 --> 00:07:27,046
Tony Stark.

214
00:07:27,179 --> 00:07:30,182
Tony Stark. I'm Tony. Let's go.

215
00:07:30,350 --> 00:07:32,284
Nice to meet you, Tony.

216
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,585
Nice to meet you.

217
00:07:34,387 --> 00:07:37,255
Is there anywhere we can grab some coffee?

218
00:07:37,824 --> 00:07:39,391
To go.

219
00:07:39,392 --> 00:07:40,692
- Coffee.
- Okay?

220
00:07:42,596 --> 00:07:44,631
The great thing about a private taxi.

221
00:07:45,198 --> 00:07:48,001
You guys woke up late,
but you got ready so fast.

222
00:07:49,836 --> 00:07:50,803
- Us?
- Yeah.

223
00:07:50,904 --> 00:07:53,205
There wasn't really much to do.

224
00:07:53,373 --> 00:07:54,606
Did you just wash your face?

225
00:07:54,607 --> 00:07:55,575
Yeah. I just washed my face...

226
00:07:55,576 --> 00:07:58,143
and threw my stuff in a corner.

227
00:07:58,779 --> 00:08:01,080
I woke up at 6:30 this morning.

228
00:08:02,115 --> 00:08:04,016
It didn't take me long to get ready.

229
00:08:05,685 --> 00:08:08,053
I love that I can just do my makeup
on the way.

230
00:08:08,462 --> 00:08:12,031
- The AC feels great too.
- It's so efficient.

231
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,292
I love it.

232
00:08:13,293 --> 00:08:14,393
(Thanks to Won Ji,
they can do their makeup in peace.)

233
00:08:14,394 --> 00:08:15,928
If you want to do your makeup,
just let me know.

234
00:08:15,929 --> 00:08:16,762
Okay.

235
00:08:17,130 --> 00:08:19,165
I want to try hot girl makeup next time.

236
00:08:19,566 --> 00:08:21,233
Being a hot girl is
all about the attitude.

237
00:08:21,234 --> 00:08:22,802
- Really?
- For a hot girl, yeah.

238
00:08:22,803 --> 00:08:23,635
How so?

239
00:08:24,104 --> 00:08:26,972
- Even the way you walk is different.
- Different?

240
00:08:26,973 --> 00:08:28,373
Down to the way you breathe.

241
00:08:28,374 --> 00:08:30,275
- You have to breathe differently too?
- Exactly.

242
00:08:30,276 --> 00:08:31,643
You have to move your hands like this too.

243
00:08:31,644 --> 00:08:34,846
Always keep your fingers extended long.

244
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:36,047
Try it.

245
00:08:36,316 --> 00:08:37,549
Like this?

246
00:08:37,951 --> 00:08:40,919
Even the way you look at people
and talk is different.

247
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:43,656
Even when you stop abruptly,
you need to know how to pose.

248
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:46,258
(Stiff...)

249
00:08:46,283 --> 00:08:47,359
(as a board)

250
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,628
(Let's take it one step at a time.)

251
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:52,865
There are way more motorcycles
than I expected.

252
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:54,867
People commute on them.

253
00:08:55,769 --> 00:08:58,104
They're all riding
with their girlfriends on the back.

254
00:08:58,772 --> 00:08:59,939
That's kind of romantic.

255
00:09:00,507 --> 00:09:03,042
Either with a girlfriend on the back
or a daughter in front.

256
00:09:05,912 --> 00:09:07,546
Maybe I should wave to him.

257
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:08,614
Hello!

258
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:10,482
Should I say hi?

259
00:09:12,118 --> 00:09:13,852
(Curious)

260
00:09:14,187 --> 00:09:15,120
Hello.

261
00:09:15,722 --> 00:09:17,156
Thank you.

262
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:19,525
(Bowing)

263
00:09:19,526 --> 00:09:20,626
Thank you.

264
00:09:20,794 --> 00:09:21,661
(Laughing)

265
00:09:21,662 --> 00:09:22,628
She seems shy.

266
00:09:22,629 --> 00:09:23,662
That's cute.

267
00:09:24,597 --> 00:09:26,798
Hello. That's how they commute to work.

268
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,067
Hello.

269
00:09:29,536 --> 00:09:31,670
- She's struggling.
- She really is.

270
00:09:31,671 --> 00:09:33,206
I could totally see myself in her.

271
00:09:33,473 --> 00:09:34,473
It looked so hard for her.

272
00:09:34,474 --> 00:09:36,241
(Protecting her fellow introverts)

273
00:09:37,677 --> 00:09:39,945
Gabee, have you done Secret Santa before?

274
00:09:39,946 --> 00:09:41,380
Right. Secret buddies.

275
00:09:41,848 --> 00:09:43,415
I've always wanted to do it,

276
00:09:44,651 --> 00:09:46,085
but I never really got the chance.

277
00:09:46,853 --> 00:09:48,754
I've always wanted to try it too.

278
00:09:51,291 --> 00:09:55,094
(While checking out
the new QR code last night)

279
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:57,630
Why don't we get valuable items...

280
00:09:57,631 --> 00:09:58,631
for our secret buddies?

281
00:09:58,998 --> 00:10:00,408
(And so, they chose their secret buddies.)

282
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:02,702
(Now for the reveal.)

283
00:10:03,236 --> 00:10:05,371
- Reveal yours here.
- Okay.

284
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:08,087
(Secret Santas are Won Ji and Gabee,
and Lee Sian and Harimu.)

285
00:10:08,408 --> 00:10:09,943
Then let's each...

286
00:10:10,543 --> 00:10:11,811
share what's on our minds.

287
00:10:12,212 --> 00:10:14,714
I love it. It's so practical.

288
00:10:14,814 --> 00:10:16,216
- It's practical, right?
- Yes.

289
00:10:16,801 --> 00:10:18,689
To my Secret Santa.

290
00:10:18,881 --> 00:10:19,886
(Sneaking a glance)

291
00:10:20,868 --> 00:10:24,220
What I need is...

292
00:10:24,221 --> 00:10:25,892
- You need something?
- What is it?

293
00:10:25,903 --> 00:10:27,197
If you'd look over here,

294
00:10:27,221 --> 00:10:29,262
I'm using selfie mode...

295
00:10:29,596 --> 00:10:31,064
to put on my makeup.

296
00:10:33,454 --> 00:10:36,230
(Message received)

297
00:10:36,657 --> 00:10:37,804
(Want to use this?)

298
00:10:37,930 --> 00:10:40,617
- Wait, are you my Secret Santa?
- No.

299
00:10:40,618 --> 00:10:42,297
I just have a lot of mirrors.

300
00:10:42,337 --> 00:10:43,676
- Really?
- Yes.

301
00:10:43,697 --> 00:10:45,948
- Did you hear that, Secret Santa?
- Did you get that?

302
00:10:45,949 --> 00:10:48,414
Hye Rim's buddy, did you hear that?

303
00:10:48,415 --> 00:10:50,517
I doubt Hye Rim is her own Secret Santa.

304
00:10:50,783 --> 00:10:52,986
I'm not feeling great about this.

305
00:10:52,987 --> 00:10:53,653
Why?

306
00:10:53,727 --> 00:10:57,423
I only packed plain shirts for this trip.

307
00:10:57,553 --> 00:10:58,432
(Putting on an act)

308
00:10:58,433 --> 00:11:00,760
I need something
that's going to lift my mood.

309
00:11:00,793 --> 00:11:02,993
(Message loud and clear)

310
00:11:03,207 --> 00:11:07,053
I'm more of a peacock,
but I packed such plain clothes.

311
00:11:07,173 --> 00:11:09,212
Did her Secret Santa hear that?

312
00:11:09,213 --> 00:11:10,937
I need something exciting.

313
00:11:10,938 --> 00:11:13,306
- She needs a mood-lifting gift.
- Exactly.

314
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,441
What about Gabee?

315
00:11:16,543 --> 00:11:18,111
Can I be honest?

316
00:11:18,112 --> 00:11:19,212
Yes.

317
00:11:19,469 --> 00:11:21,489
(Honest?)

318
00:11:21,714 --> 00:11:23,714
Gabee needs a razor.

319
00:11:24,629 --> 00:11:26,252
Can we share one?

320
00:11:26,796 --> 00:11:28,228
For my legs.

321
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:30,043
- I didn't expect to wear shorts.
- Me neither.

322
00:11:30,044 --> 00:11:31,090
- So...
- Me neither.

323
00:11:31,823 --> 00:11:36,162
I feel like we could all use one.

324
00:11:36,462 --> 00:11:39,616
- Let's buy one later then.
- For everyone.

325
00:11:39,617 --> 00:11:40,836
Let's grab one at a convenience store.

326
00:11:40,837 --> 00:11:42,502
What I need is...

327
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:44,704
I like things that make sounds.

328
00:11:44,816 --> 00:11:46,315
- Things that make sounds?
- Like...

329
00:11:46,316 --> 00:11:48,408
that wooden temple block
Hye Rim mentioned.

330
00:11:48,482 --> 00:11:50,709
- A music box?
- Or a music box.

331
00:11:50,757 --> 00:11:52,779
- I like stuff like that.
- So that's your thing.

332
00:11:53,215 --> 00:11:54,382
As for me,

333
00:11:54,647 --> 00:11:56,783
I've grown so fond
of elephants in Thailand.

334
00:11:56,784 --> 00:11:58,284
- Elephants?
- Yes.

335
00:11:58,285 --> 00:12:00,353
I want some elephant merch.

336
00:12:00,437 --> 00:12:02,617
They're so cute.
I've grown to love them too.

337
00:12:02,618 --> 00:12:04,824
- Elephants are cute.
- I've grown to love them too.

338
00:12:05,491 --> 00:12:06,726
A girl who loves elephants.

339
00:12:06,727 --> 00:12:07,827
Perfect for Bangkok.

340
00:12:10,505 --> 00:12:12,098
An elephant lover.

341
00:12:12,099 --> 00:12:15,011
- Elephant lover.
- Yes, you're an elephant lover.

342
00:12:15,525 --> 00:12:17,298
(You got that, my Secret Santa?)

343
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:21,906
(Getting to know each other better)

344
00:12:23,090 --> 00:12:25,149
(At a nearby fast-food place for coffee)

345
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:26,112
Coffee.

346
00:12:26,957 --> 00:12:29,522
Then let me go grab us some breakfast...

347
00:12:29,523 --> 00:12:31,451
- just something simple.
- I'd love that.

348
00:12:31,836 --> 00:12:33,298
Thank you.

349
00:12:33,853 --> 00:12:35,853
Our outfits are so cute.

350
00:12:36,263 --> 00:12:38,357
(Today's dress code:
four elephant sisters)

351
00:12:38,625 --> 00:12:40,482
Meow, meow, meow, meow.

352
00:12:40,483 --> 00:12:43,129
(Entering in a friendly conga line)

353
00:12:44,343 --> 00:12:46,825
It's corn pie! I really love corn pie.

354
00:12:46,826 --> 00:12:48,201
- Let's eat this first.
- Let's do it.

355
00:12:48,363 --> 00:12:50,570
They don't have this in Korea right now.

356
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:54,772
If it's good, maybe I'll order one too.

357
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:57,777
It's so good. It's totally my style.

358
00:12:58,444 --> 00:12:59,812
Can I grab this one?

359
00:13:01,353 --> 00:13:03,513
(Gabee doesn't forget
her favorite corn pie.)

360
00:13:03,747 --> 00:13:06,579
(The others follow suit and order.)

361
00:13:06,706 --> 00:13:09,455
One bestseller, please.

362
00:13:09,733 --> 00:13:12,733
(Treasurer Harimu pays at the end.)

363
00:13:12,734 --> 00:13:14,627
Should we get our driver a coffee?

364
00:13:14,628 --> 00:13:15,628
Sounds good.

365
00:13:15,928 --> 00:13:18,598
- Let's get him a meal set.
- Great idea.

366
00:13:20,107 --> 00:13:22,168
Nice. She's such a great treasurer.

367
00:13:22,169 --> 00:13:23,940
(Day 2 group fund:
breakfast 1,069 baht, about 49 dollars)

368
00:13:24,522 --> 00:13:26,906
Our treasurer has long nails,
but she counts cash so fast.

369
00:13:28,041 --> 00:13:30,209
It's fascinating.
She handles bills so well.

370
00:13:30,543 --> 00:13:32,245
Handling money feels great.

371
00:13:33,713 --> 00:13:35,968
- We ordered a lot, didn't we?
- I'm starving.

372
00:13:35,969 --> 00:13:37,015
(Enjoy your meal.)

373
00:13:37,555 --> 00:13:39,285
- Let me grab it.
- Okay.

374
00:13:39,286 --> 00:13:40,828
(Loaded up, driver's order delivered)

375
00:13:41,054 --> 00:13:44,757
I can't get over this corn pie.

376
00:13:45,591 --> 00:13:47,260
This corn pie is so good.

377
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,730
- Breakfast is here.
- Try the corn pie.

378
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,165
- Isn't it good?
- Corn pie.

379
00:13:52,506 --> 00:13:53,619
(Munching)

380
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:55,435
It's so good. Sian's loving it.

381
00:13:55,544 --> 00:13:56,790
- I'm happy.
- So good.

382
00:13:56,791 --> 00:13:58,971
I love seeing them
enjoy something I picked.

383
00:13:58,972 --> 00:14:00,073
That's the best feeling.

384
00:14:01,191 --> 00:14:03,343
(She might come back to Thailand
just for corn pie.)

385
00:14:03,744 --> 00:14:04,997
(Her face says it all.)

386
00:14:04,998 --> 00:14:06,179
(Isn't this insane?)

387
00:14:07,491 --> 00:14:09,651
(Sharing the good stuff with everyone)

388
00:14:09,652 --> 00:14:10,516
It's delicious.

389
00:14:10,711 --> 00:14:12,618
- Girl.
- Eat the best part.

390
00:14:12,985 --> 00:14:16,356
It's corn-flavored custard cream.

391
00:14:16,357 --> 00:14:17,457
(Savoring the flavor)

392
00:14:17,536 --> 00:14:20,526
Food makes me so happy.

393
00:14:20,696 --> 00:14:22,161
It feels like a picnic.

394
00:14:22,783 --> 00:14:24,623
(Her whole body says it's delicious.)

395
00:14:24,970 --> 00:14:27,367
Earlier, I packed my suitcase...

396
00:14:27,368 --> 00:14:30,370
in a total rush without much thought.

397
00:14:30,937 --> 00:14:32,605
I barely packed a thing.

398
00:14:34,107 --> 00:14:35,775
But the trip still works out fine.
It's so easy.

399
00:14:35,776 --> 00:14:36,876
- Right.
- It's actually better.

400
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,011
- No choices to make.
- Right.

401
00:14:39,012 --> 00:14:40,403
- No deciding what to wear.
- You can just...

402
00:14:40,404 --> 00:14:42,404
focus on the trip itself.

403
00:14:42,534 --> 00:14:43,216
Right.

404
00:14:43,217 --> 00:14:45,318
It's so fine once you just let go.

405
00:14:45,476 --> 00:14:48,221
- Normally I'd want sneakers...
- Right.

406
00:14:48,362 --> 00:14:50,723
- and heels just in case.
- Of course.

407
00:14:50,882 --> 00:14:51,958
Right.

408
00:14:53,259 --> 00:14:56,322
But once you decide
"I'm only wearing these two,"

409
00:14:56,323 --> 00:14:58,323
- it gets so much easier.
- It's so freeing.

410
00:14:58,846 --> 00:15:00,392
(The carefree single-outfit look)

411
00:15:00,393 --> 00:15:01,467
- Next time...
- Okay.

412
00:15:01,913 --> 00:15:05,420
if you travel again,
would you pack this light?

413
00:15:05,421 --> 00:15:07,073
One hundred percent.

414
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:08,441
Me too, 100 percent.

415
00:15:08,841 --> 00:15:10,510
It was so nice once I actually tried it.

416
00:15:10,711 --> 00:15:11,577
- Right.
- Me too.

417
00:15:12,145 --> 00:15:13,579
Why did we ever...

418
00:15:14,531 --> 00:15:16,849
travel with up to three suitcases?

419
00:15:18,451 --> 00:15:19,752
This feels so nice.

420
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:22,221
I'm full, cool, and happy.

421
00:15:22,222 --> 00:15:24,995
(After some self-reflection,
they feel warm inside.)

422
00:15:25,175 --> 00:15:28,194
The sun isn't beating down today.

423
00:15:29,155 --> 00:15:31,028
- That's nice.
- Maybe it won't get too hot.

424
00:15:31,109 --> 00:15:33,029
Then it shouldn't be so hot.

425
00:15:35,429 --> 00:15:37,629
Thank you, Buddha.

426
00:15:37,789 --> 00:15:40,062
(A chance encounter with Buddha)

427
00:15:40,282 --> 00:15:42,008
I even celebrated Buddha's birthday.

428
00:15:42,009 --> 00:15:44,329
(Merciful weather deepens their faith.)

429
00:15:44,482 --> 00:15:46,112
Isn't this a Buddhist country?

430
00:15:46,546 --> 00:15:49,849
About 93 to 95 percent
of the people are Buddhist.

431
00:15:49,890 --> 00:15:50,730
Really?

432
00:15:50,731 --> 00:15:52,731
The land of Buddha.

433
00:15:52,877 --> 00:15:54,520
The rest are Christians
and other religions.

434
00:15:54,744 --> 00:15:58,729
Under the constitution,
the king has to be Buddhist.

435
00:15:59,358 --> 00:16:01,194
It's not strictly just Buddhism, though.

436
00:16:01,472 --> 00:16:04,664
Buddhism mixes with Hinduism
and local folk beliefs.

437
00:16:04,665 --> 00:16:07,700
On the streets and outside buildings,

438
00:16:07,701 --> 00:16:10,837
you'll see tiny spirit houses
called san phra phum...

439
00:16:11,145 --> 00:16:13,292
decorated with flowers.

440
00:16:13,552 --> 00:16:16,442
Every home has one out front.

441
00:16:17,577 --> 00:16:19,679
- Right. I saw those.
- There were so many.

442
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:21,313
(Spirit houses are
a common sight outside.)

443
00:16:22,101 --> 00:16:24,517
What's everyone's favorite food?

444
00:16:24,518 --> 00:16:25,918
- Favorite?
- Rice noodles for me.

445
00:16:26,853 --> 00:16:27,787
Pho!

446
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,485
- I love soups and broths.
- Me too.

447
00:16:30,486 --> 00:16:31,858
- Soups and broths?
- Yes.

448
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:32,792
I love tteokbokki.

449
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:34,227
That's cute.

450
00:16:34,886 --> 00:16:37,930
I can't eat much tteokbokki
these days, though.

451
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:39,732
It's hard for me to digest.

452
00:16:40,246 --> 00:16:42,735
You felt sick on the first day.

453
00:16:42,906 --> 00:16:44,704
Has digestion always been
an issue for you?

454
00:16:45,404 --> 00:16:46,839
No, right before coming here,

455
00:16:47,115 --> 00:16:48,730
I thought I should eat
a ton of Korean food,

456
00:16:48,755 --> 00:16:50,710
so I overate and got terrible indigestion.

457
00:16:51,314 --> 00:16:55,114
It made me realize I should eat it
while my body can still process it.

458
00:16:55,994 --> 00:16:58,851
Eat plenty of tteokbokki
while you can still digest it.

459
00:16:59,734 --> 00:17:00,887
(Life wisdom gained)

460
00:17:00,888 --> 00:17:01,854
Jjajangmyeon too.

461
00:17:01,927 --> 00:17:04,247
Foods packed with flour...

462
00:17:04,248 --> 00:17:06,192
They can feel so heavy on your stomach.

463
00:17:06,626 --> 00:17:08,628
Army stew sounds so good right now too.

464
00:17:08,629 --> 00:17:09,875
(A free-flowing chat)

465
00:17:10,229 --> 00:17:12,695
(A seafood market. Food.)

466
00:17:12,696 --> 00:17:14,033
Are we eating seafood today?

467
00:17:15,268 --> 00:17:17,503
I don't think they sell seafood there.

468
00:17:17,562 --> 00:17:18,504
Really?

469
00:17:18,602 --> 00:17:20,640
It's more like a river than the ocean.

470
00:17:21,895 --> 00:17:25,144
People ride around
in these canoe-like boats...

471
00:17:26,279 --> 00:17:27,713
buying and selling things.

472
00:17:28,737 --> 00:17:29,749
That's so fascinating.

473
00:17:30,016 --> 00:17:31,717
We'll definitely need some time to shop.

474
00:17:32,718 --> 00:17:34,120
I think we're here.

475
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:35,488
This is going to be fun.

476
00:17:35,489 --> 00:17:39,681
(The market entrance appears
as they chat.)

477
00:17:41,027 --> 00:17:42,795
Thank you, Tony.

478
00:17:42,855 --> 00:17:44,861
Thank you.

479
00:17:45,298 --> 00:17:46,732
Let's grab the suitcase.

480
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:47,900
- Okay.
- The suitcase.

481
00:17:48,834 --> 00:17:50,269
Our beloved suitcase.

482
00:17:52,314 --> 00:17:54,142
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

483
00:17:54,166 --> 00:17:55,900
- I'll wheel it.
- Thank you.

484
00:17:56,175 --> 00:17:58,711
This is the floating market.

485
00:17:58,888 --> 00:17:59,841
The flirting market?

486
00:17:59,842 --> 00:18:01,714
Yes, the flirting market.

487
00:18:01,715 --> 00:18:04,116
Flirt all you want in there.

488
00:18:04,117 --> 00:18:06,231
(Bargain and flirt all you want.)

489
00:18:06,351 --> 00:18:09,717
Do a lot of tourists come here?

490
00:18:09,718 --> 00:18:13,893
It's a must-see spot outside the city.

491
00:18:18,697 --> 00:18:20,977
(Damnoen Saduak)

492
00:18:22,457 --> 00:18:25,630
(Thailand's most famous floating market
with over 150 years of history)

493
00:18:25,937 --> 00:18:29,103
(Cruising through the canals by boat)

494
00:18:29,477 --> 00:18:32,657
(Shopping and eating all at once)

495
00:18:33,130 --> 00:18:35,983
(A unique attraction
offering a special experience)

496
00:18:38,584 --> 00:18:40,584
Sunlight!

497
00:18:41,167 --> 00:18:43,167
I was totally wrong
about there being no sun.

498
00:18:44,822 --> 00:18:46,592
I can barely open my eyes.

499
00:18:47,059 --> 00:18:50,329
I don't have sunglasses
in my personal bag.

500
00:18:50,369 --> 00:18:51,497
Personal bag.

501
00:18:51,764 --> 00:18:54,153
Still, the humidity feels way lower today.

502
00:18:54,154 --> 00:18:56,569
- It really does.
- Right?

503
00:18:56,816 --> 00:18:58,170
It's so pretty.

504
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,960
Look over here. Stand right here.

505
00:19:00,961 --> 00:19:03,142
- Should we take a group photo?
- Let's do it.

506
00:19:03,307 --> 00:19:05,011
Get in the shot too.

507
00:19:05,378 --> 00:19:08,781
- This suitcase is coming in so clutch.
- Harimu, come over here.

508
00:19:09,015 --> 00:19:12,284
How do you do the "it girl" pose?

509
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:13,686
First, pop your hip out.

510
00:19:13,813 --> 00:19:14,920
Pop it way out.

511
00:19:14,921 --> 00:19:15,955
Then bend a little right here.

512
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:17,056
Your right foot.

513
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:18,524
My right foot?

514
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:20,832
- Then tuck your elbow in.
- Like this?

515
00:19:20,833 --> 00:19:22,595
Hold it up like this. Perfect.

516
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,330
- Nice.
- Okay.

517
00:19:24,380 --> 00:19:25,297
Bend it.

518
00:19:25,333 --> 00:19:26,399
It girls!

519
00:19:26,613 --> 00:19:27,800
Three, two...

520
00:19:28,373 --> 00:19:30,403
- It turned out amazing.
- It really did.

521
00:19:30,506 --> 00:19:31,904
The photo looks great.

522
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,592
Pretty!

523
00:19:35,593 --> 00:19:37,447
(Instant energy boost)

524
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:40,547
(A good photo instantly lifts their mood.)

525
00:19:40,693 --> 00:19:41,900
(Now for the other side)

526
00:19:44,893 --> 00:19:46,500
(It girl malfunction)

527
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,621
I guess I'm just not cut out
to be an "it girl."

528
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:50,556
"That girl," "it girl," or "hot girl"...

529
00:19:50,557 --> 00:19:52,491
- any girl works!
- Right.

530
00:19:53,592 --> 00:19:54,393
Okay.

531
00:19:54,827 --> 00:19:55,795
Here we go.

532
00:19:55,867 --> 00:19:57,229
Finally, the floating market.

533
00:19:57,670 --> 00:20:00,366
- Damnoen Saduak.
- So this is it!

534
00:20:01,076 --> 00:20:03,010
- Look, fans!
- Over there.

535
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:05,003
Those fans look so nice.

536
00:20:05,671 --> 00:20:07,472
That fan is huge.

537
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:11,242
(Captivating the quartet are
colorful shops along the canal.)

538
00:20:11,243 --> 00:20:13,645
Let's buy something here.

539
00:20:14,113 --> 00:20:17,015
That hat with the "Thailand" logo
looks cool.

540
00:20:17,583 --> 00:20:18,950
I need to get a gift for my Secret Santa.

541
00:20:18,951 --> 00:20:19,817
(They have everything.)

542
00:20:19,818 --> 00:20:22,086
I like that tote bag too.

543
00:20:22,087 --> 00:20:23,454
There's one with an elephant down there.

544
00:20:23,455 --> 00:20:24,622
The one on the edge.

545
00:20:24,623 --> 00:20:25,890
It's my style.

546
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:26,791
(Sian's pick)

547
00:20:26,792 --> 00:20:28,227
Is my Secret Santa listening?

548
00:20:28,794 --> 00:20:30,228
Is she listening?

549
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,028
(Definitely.)

550
00:20:31,330 --> 00:20:33,431
Look at that hat.

551
00:20:33,432 --> 00:20:34,532
It's totally my style.

552
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:37,101
- It's so cute, right?
- So cute.

553
00:20:37,102 --> 00:20:38,703
(Packed with cute accessories)

554
00:20:38,728 --> 00:20:41,997
I want to shop here.

555
00:20:42,275 --> 00:20:43,518
I'm ready to burn a hole in my pocket.

556
00:20:43,543 --> 00:20:45,476
There are shops over here too.

557
00:20:45,477 --> 00:20:46,378
(Shops line the canal as well.)

558
00:20:47,179 --> 00:20:48,079
This is it.

559
00:20:48,314 --> 00:20:49,214
Here it is.

560
00:20:49,949 --> 00:20:51,683
I like this.

561
00:20:51,684 --> 00:20:52,550
(Foldable hats spotted)

562
00:20:52,551 --> 00:20:54,953
Isn't this so cute?

563
00:20:55,922 --> 00:20:57,289
You can wear it like this.

564
00:20:57,823 --> 00:20:59,023
It works as a fan too.

565
00:20:59,024 --> 00:21:00,925
It's a fan-hat.

566
00:21:00,950 --> 00:21:02,871
(Fold it to fan, unfold to wear.)

567
00:21:02,896 --> 00:21:05,196
This is so smart.

568
00:21:05,197 --> 00:21:06,064
Okay.

569
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:08,033
We definitely have to buy this.

570
00:21:08,034 --> 00:21:09,735
These hats are perfect for us.

571
00:21:09,736 --> 00:21:10,769
They're so cute.

572
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:11,804
They're so compact.

573
00:21:11,805 --> 00:21:12,938
Should we buy these?

574
00:21:13,577 --> 00:21:16,274
- I can't believe this.
- This is unbelievable.

575
00:21:16,609 --> 00:21:18,777
Yes, totally.

576
00:21:19,178 --> 00:21:21,933
(Completely awestruck)

577
00:21:23,315 --> 00:21:24,148
This is awesome.

578
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:25,783
Look at that.

579
00:21:26,986 --> 00:21:29,121
- Should we ask how much it is?
- I like this yellow one.

580
00:21:29,355 --> 00:21:31,156
Pretend you don't like it that much.

581
00:21:31,157 --> 00:21:33,091
Right, we need to play it cool.

582
00:21:33,426 --> 00:21:35,260
How much are these?

583
00:21:35,261 --> 00:21:36,895
(Asking nonchalantly)

584
00:21:37,263 --> 00:21:38,063
Two hundred?

585
00:21:39,098 --> 00:21:40,034
(Sighing)

586
00:21:40,035 --> 00:21:42,267
- That's too expensive.
- Expensive.

587
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:44,602
(Desperate pleas for a discount)

588
00:21:45,204 --> 00:21:46,037
We're getting four.

589
00:21:46,038 --> 00:21:47,905
(Sian boldly offers 100 baht,
about 5 dollars)

590
00:21:47,906 --> 00:21:49,473
We'll take four of them.

591
00:21:49,775 --> 00:21:51,809
(First bargain failed.)

592
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:52,877
Four.

593
00:21:52,878 --> 00:21:53,811
How about 110 baht then?

594
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:54,912
Okay.

595
00:21:55,548 --> 00:21:58,150
(I can give you about 50 cents more.)

596
00:21:59,018 --> 00:22:00,451
(All right, 110 it is.)

597
00:22:00,452 --> 00:22:02,287
Okay, 110 isn't too bad.

598
00:22:02,288 --> 00:22:03,869
(Wait, this actually worked?)

599
00:22:04,090 --> 00:22:07,526
(Celebrating the successful bargain)

600
00:22:07,927 --> 00:22:09,594
(Taking their time choosing hats)

601
00:22:09,595 --> 00:22:10,863
The blue ones are pretty too.

602
00:22:11,096 --> 00:22:12,597
You look so pretty.

603
00:22:12,832 --> 00:22:15,500
Thank you. You too.

604
00:22:15,501 --> 00:22:17,703
This looks nice. I'll go with this one.

605
00:22:17,704 --> 00:22:19,304
(Sian picks a mint hat.)

606
00:22:19,305 --> 00:22:20,539
All right.

607
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:22,575
Doesn't yellow look great on me?

608
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:25,143
(Hat hunt: successful)

609
00:22:25,144 --> 00:22:26,577
This is so avant-garde.

610
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:29,981
What if we get scouted?

611
00:22:30,216 --> 00:22:31,750
We're all going to be stars.

612
00:22:31,751 --> 00:22:32,751
Of course.

613
00:22:34,253 --> 00:22:35,553
One, two...

614
00:22:36,255 --> 00:22:38,223
(Hot Four ready to make
their Thailand debut)

615
00:22:38,625 --> 00:22:41,526
I love traveling with Won Ji.

616
00:22:41,527 --> 00:22:43,895
I love traveling with Won Ji.

617
00:22:44,296 --> 00:22:45,863
I've reached a whole new level.

618
00:22:46,732 --> 00:22:47,699
(Can't believe what she's hearing)

619
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:49,701
What is she saying?

620
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:54,839
(Back to the docks)

621
00:22:55,383 --> 00:22:58,285
- The prices aren't as bad as I thought.
- They're not bad.

622
00:22:58,310 --> 00:22:59,110
Here it is.

623
00:22:59,311 --> 00:23:02,079
- Hello.
- Hello.

624
00:23:02,849 --> 00:23:04,017
It's 500 baht for one boat.

625
00:23:04,150 --> 00:23:05,283
Is it 500?

626
00:23:05,452 --> 00:23:07,085
Let's use our shared fund.

627
00:23:07,086 --> 00:23:09,387
- We're using the group fund.
- Good.

628
00:23:09,955 --> 00:23:11,322
(Remaining balance: 3,732 baht)

629
00:23:11,323 --> 00:23:12,857
Four tickets, please.

630
00:23:12,858 --> 00:23:13,658
Okay.

631
00:23:13,759 --> 00:23:15,092
Thank you.

632
00:23:15,093 --> 00:23:16,394
Okay, let's go.

633
00:23:16,395 --> 00:23:18,629
- Let's go!
- That's the boarding gate.

634
00:23:19,032 --> 00:23:20,766
What if this boat capsizes?

635
00:23:22,768 --> 00:23:25,337
(The boat for the four)

636
00:23:25,338 --> 00:23:26,471
It looks fun, though.

637
00:23:26,939 --> 00:23:28,139
This is so cool.

638
00:23:28,307 --> 00:23:29,674
(Wow)

639
00:23:30,109 --> 00:23:31,676
This won't capsize, will it?

640
00:23:32,211 --> 00:23:33,211
It might.

641
00:23:33,212 --> 00:23:35,446
We need to put our luggage inside too.

642
00:23:35,815 --> 00:23:37,983
Put it up in the front.

643
00:23:38,751 --> 00:23:40,285
All right, it's in.

644
00:23:40,286 --> 00:23:41,886
(Bag safely loaded up front)

645
00:23:42,388 --> 00:23:43,521
(Next up: Gabee)

646
00:23:43,522 --> 00:23:45,023
(Groans)

647
00:23:45,024 --> 00:23:45,890
I'm scared.

648
00:23:46,192 --> 00:23:47,358
Careful.

649
00:23:49,962 --> 00:23:50,795
(Wobbling)

650
00:23:51,330 --> 00:23:52,197
(The boat rocks.)

651
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:53,998
(Rattle rattle)

652
00:23:53,999 --> 00:23:55,433
(Clang)

653
00:23:56,001 --> 00:23:58,402
(Our precious bag!)

654
00:23:58,403 --> 00:23:59,170
Wait.

655
00:23:59,371 --> 00:24:00,938
Wait.

656
00:24:01,274 --> 00:24:02,040
Wait.

657
00:24:02,041 --> 00:24:03,275
Wait, I'm getting on.

658
00:24:03,276 --> 00:24:05,576
Try to balance your weight.

659
00:24:05,577 --> 00:24:06,878
(The older duo getting dramatic)

660
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:08,079
This is so scary.

661
00:24:08,514 --> 00:24:09,348
Okay.

662
00:24:09,589 --> 00:24:10,882
Let's go.

663
00:24:11,284 --> 00:24:12,484
Keep your foot right there.

664
00:24:12,719 --> 00:24:13,885
This actually works.

665
00:24:13,886 --> 00:24:17,622
(The younger duo gets on effortlessly.)

666
00:24:18,023 --> 00:24:20,424
Yes, we made it!

667
00:24:20,425 --> 00:24:22,360
(Finally ready to set off)

668
00:24:22,461 --> 00:24:23,261
Let's go.

669
00:24:23,762 --> 00:24:26,931
Hi! Welcome to Thailand.

670
00:24:27,366 --> 00:24:31,102
- Okay, let's go!
- Let's go.

671
00:24:35,074 --> 00:24:36,808
Are we shopping here?

672
00:24:36,809 --> 00:24:38,576
Of course. Grab something to eat...

673
00:24:38,745 --> 00:24:39,820
or whatever you want.

674
00:24:39,845 --> 00:24:41,946
I can already see some interesting stuff.

675
00:24:42,848 --> 00:24:43,648
Look.

676
00:24:44,250 --> 00:24:46,318
Isn't that tote bag so cute?

677
00:24:48,487 --> 00:24:50,089
That Buddha statue is cute.

678
00:24:50,090 --> 00:24:50,889
(Come on over.)

679
00:24:51,223 --> 00:24:52,623
No, no.

680
00:24:54,159 --> 00:24:56,694
I'm just going to grab a drink.

681
00:24:56,695 --> 00:24:58,596
(The shopkeeper reeling them in)

682
00:24:59,231 --> 00:25:01,833
(Getting hooked, literally)

683
00:25:01,834 --> 00:25:03,034
I'm just getting a drink.

684
00:25:04,003 --> 00:25:05,236
They're reeling us in!

685
00:25:05,237 --> 00:25:06,872
Pulling us right in.

686
00:25:07,178 --> 00:25:07,873
(Hit)

687
00:25:09,008 --> 00:25:10,341
What's happening?

688
00:25:10,342 --> 00:25:13,144
Look, she's actually pulling us in.

689
00:25:13,145 --> 00:25:14,579
This is crazy.

690
00:25:15,047 --> 00:25:17,015
Come on.

691
00:25:17,016 --> 00:25:17,949
Come on.

692
00:25:18,083 --> 00:25:20,651
We're heading somewhere else.

693
00:25:21,554 --> 00:25:23,588
(Letting go)

694
00:25:23,589 --> 00:25:25,590
- Bye!
- Thank you.

695
00:25:25,591 --> 00:25:28,226
"You guys aren't going to buy anything."

696
00:25:28,327 --> 00:25:31,362
She's still pretty chill about it.

697
00:25:31,497 --> 00:25:33,331
It's fun coming back after so long.

698
00:25:36,702 --> 00:25:39,203
- What are you eating?
- What's that?

699
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:40,605
What is that?

700
00:25:41,340 --> 00:25:42,407
- Is it good?
- Noodles?

701
00:25:42,741 --> 00:25:44,542
Are those noodles?

702
00:25:44,543 --> 00:25:46,111
They're selling skewers too.

703
00:25:46,558 --> 00:25:47,922
(Grilled right on the boat)

704
00:25:47,947 --> 00:25:48,947
It smells so good.

705
00:25:49,157 --> 00:25:51,525
They're cooking right on their boats.

706
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:52,850
Don't they get scared?

707
00:25:52,851 --> 00:25:54,362
(Cooking effortlessly on the boat)

708
00:25:54,387 --> 00:25:55,887
- They're one with the boat.
- I know, right?

709
00:25:56,989 --> 00:25:58,756
What are those, Won Ji?

710
00:25:58,757 --> 00:25:59,924
(Green mangoes:
known for their crisp, sour flavor)

711
00:25:59,925 --> 00:26:01,493
Those are a firmer type of mango.

712
00:26:02,094 --> 00:26:03,694
Looks like they mostly sell fruit.

713
00:26:03,695 --> 00:26:04,595
(A street food paradise)

714
00:26:05,437 --> 00:26:07,065
I know what they're eating!

715
00:26:07,166 --> 00:26:08,199
Coconut ice cream!

716
00:26:08,634 --> 00:26:10,602
- We have to get one.
- I see it right over there.

717
00:26:10,603 --> 00:26:12,103
Oh, is this the place?

718
00:26:12,439 --> 00:26:13,905
Come to mama, coconut!

719
00:26:15,007 --> 00:26:17,008
We'd like an ice cream.

720
00:26:17,009 --> 00:26:17,976
Just one?

721
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:19,777
Let's just get one to share.

722
00:26:19,778 --> 00:26:21,011
(Getting one to share)

723
00:26:21,012 --> 00:26:21,979
Yes, just one.

724
00:26:22,548 --> 00:26:25,650
- Extra, please!
- A lot.

725
00:26:25,651 --> 00:26:28,019
(Begging for extra)

726
00:26:28,020 --> 00:26:29,587
Go for it, girl!

727
00:26:30,322 --> 00:26:32,223
I was hoping for an extra scoop.

728
00:26:32,224 --> 00:26:33,325
One more scoop, please.

729
00:26:33,892 --> 00:26:37,061
(One extra scoop of sticky rice)

730
00:26:37,563 --> 00:26:41,299
(Topped with nuts)

731
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:43,434
- Thank you.
- How much is it?

732
00:26:44,703 --> 00:26:47,204
(One coconut ice cream: 60 baht,
about 3 dollars)

733
00:26:47,205 --> 00:26:49,740
Thank you, bye-bye!

734
00:26:49,909 --> 00:26:50,875
It looks so pretty.

735
00:26:51,543 --> 00:26:52,878
(The front row gets the first taste.)

736
00:26:52,879 --> 00:26:54,146
It looks so good.

737
00:26:55,914 --> 00:26:57,882
I need to film this.

738
00:27:00,152 --> 00:27:00,952
(Frozen)

739
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:01,786
Is it good?

740
00:27:02,087 --> 00:27:04,422
(Won Ji and Sian take a bite too.)

741
00:27:08,193 --> 00:27:09,960
- This is so cold.
- It's good.

742
00:27:09,961 --> 00:27:10,861
It's delicious.

743
00:27:12,564 --> 00:27:13,397
So good.

744
00:27:13,966 --> 00:27:14,832
Yes, girl.

745
00:27:17,003 --> 00:27:20,872
- It tastes like a blend of...
- Milk and coconut.

746
00:27:21,740 --> 00:27:23,874
(One more)

747
00:27:24,177 --> 00:27:25,043
Coming right up.

748
00:27:25,577 --> 00:27:26,644
(Sharing)

749
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:27,778
This is so delicious.

750
00:27:27,779 --> 00:27:29,313
Try the coconut meat.

751
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:30,214
It's so good.

752
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:37,555
(Chilled to the bone)

753
00:27:37,824 --> 00:27:39,958
What's the green rice, Gabee?

754
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:42,327
It's super sticky.

755
00:27:42,328 --> 00:27:43,928
Try it. It's rice.

756
00:27:43,929 --> 00:27:45,496
It tastes like yakbap.

757
00:27:45,931 --> 00:27:47,265
(Sticky rice similar to yakbap)

758
00:27:48,033 --> 00:27:50,301
Let me get one more bite...

759
00:27:51,303 --> 00:27:53,204
before I hand it over to you guys.

760
00:27:54,207 --> 00:27:55,674
- It's super delicious.
- Have some more.

761
00:27:57,911 --> 00:27:59,677
They have a lot of Buddha merch.

762
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:03,548
I want a golden Buddha for my house.

763
00:28:04,049 --> 00:28:05,983
(Won Ji wants one.)

764
00:28:05,984 --> 00:28:07,319
They really have everything.

765
00:28:07,719 --> 00:28:09,520
This is so cute.

766
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:10,354
(Secret Santa radar activated)

767
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:11,656
(Glance)

768
00:28:11,657 --> 00:28:12,556
So cute.

769
00:28:12,557 --> 00:28:13,957
(Noted)

770
00:28:14,527 --> 00:28:16,261
Look, they have a unique elephant.

771
00:28:16,595 --> 00:28:17,328
(Listening)

772
00:28:17,329 --> 00:28:18,615
(Note-taking on every single comment)

773
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:20,464
(Glancing around)

774
00:28:20,632 --> 00:28:23,001
The elephant is so cute.

775
00:28:23,026 --> 00:28:25,836
(The Secret Santa mind games
have already begun.)

776
00:28:26,071 --> 00:28:27,672
This elephant looks so cute.

777
00:28:27,713 --> 00:28:28,648
It's cute.

778
00:28:28,673 --> 00:28:30,142
Don't pull us in.

779
00:28:30,167 --> 00:28:31,575
Oh, they're pulling us in.

780
00:28:31,576 --> 00:28:33,377
The rattan bags are cute.

781
00:28:33,378 --> 00:28:35,013
The hats are so cute too.

782
00:28:35,915 --> 00:28:38,316
- I need to get an elephant plushie.
- A plushie?

783
00:28:39,017 --> 00:28:40,584
No, your Secret Santa will get you one.

784
00:28:40,585 --> 00:28:42,387
She can just buy me a bag.

785
00:28:43,254 --> 00:28:44,588
She's a clear communicator.

786
00:28:44,589 --> 00:28:46,657
(A buddy with very clear preferences)

787
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:47,978
Come to think of it,

788
00:28:48,003 --> 00:28:50,762
- we don't even have a small bag.
- Right, we need one.

789
00:28:50,763 --> 00:28:53,898
Do they sell tumbler pouches here?

790
00:28:54,867 --> 00:28:56,535
I see one.

791
00:28:56,536 --> 00:28:58,303
- There's a tumbler bag right there.
- It's there.

792
00:28:58,304 --> 00:29:00,738
Look, tumbler bags.

793
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:01,739
(Tumbler bag spotted)

794
00:29:02,241 --> 00:29:03,841
(Are you listening, Secret Santa?)

795
00:29:03,842 --> 00:29:05,476
I want a tumbler pouch.

796
00:29:06,011 --> 00:29:07,378
(Silence)

797
00:29:07,379 --> 00:29:09,247
- Not a single answer.
- Nobody answers.

798
00:29:09,248 --> 00:29:10,248
Right.

799
00:29:12,184 --> 00:29:14,986
Where is my Secret Santa?

800
00:29:15,454 --> 00:29:17,889
Who is her Secret Santa anyway?

801
00:29:17,890 --> 00:29:19,423
Wake up!

802
00:29:19,424 --> 00:29:21,525
(Gabee is Won Ji's Secret Santa.)

803
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:23,761
Close your eyes for five minutes.

804
00:29:24,029 --> 00:29:26,463
I can close my eyes for five minutes too.

805
00:29:26,464 --> 00:29:29,667
Try shopping like this.

806
00:29:29,668 --> 00:29:32,169
I don't think we can.
Not with everyone right here.

807
00:29:32,170 --> 00:29:33,971
I don't think we can buy anything here.

808
00:29:33,972 --> 00:29:36,607
- Let's just buy stuff for ourselves.
- Good idea.

809
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:38,803
(Arriving at the shop with tumbler bags)

810
00:29:39,211 --> 00:29:41,078
- Look!
- That looks like your type.

811
00:29:41,079 --> 00:29:45,049
(Target: lavender tumbler pouch)

812
00:29:45,951 --> 00:29:48,319
(The bargaining has already begun.)

813
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:50,488
- How much is it?
- She says 250 baht.

814
00:29:50,489 --> 00:29:51,605
Let me try knocking 100 baht off.

815
00:29:51,630 --> 00:29:52,650
"What about 150?"

816
00:29:52,858 --> 00:29:54,559
(Bargaining in Korean)

817
00:29:55,172 --> 00:29:56,736
(Pretending to leave)

818
00:29:57,079 --> 00:29:58,730
She's actually letting us walk away.

819
00:29:59,031 --> 00:30:01,299
But it's way too pretty to leave behind.

820
00:30:01,548 --> 00:30:03,484
It's fair because I didn't
use much yesterday.

821
00:30:03,485 --> 00:30:04,718
Okay, wait. Last negotiation.

822
00:30:05,006 --> 00:30:06,553
Final suggestion.

823
00:30:07,553 --> 00:30:08,856
Final suggestion, she says.

824
00:30:09,266 --> 00:30:10,190
Put 180.

825
00:30:10,758 --> 00:30:11,759
Final suggestion.

826
00:30:11,766 --> 00:30:13,493
(She is offering a final suggestion
of 180 baht.)

827
00:30:13,779 --> 00:30:14,653
Okay.

828
00:30:14,862 --> 00:30:16,166
(Her Last Suggestion worked!)

829
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:17,591
Which color?

830
00:30:17,599 --> 00:30:19,099
(Negotiation was successful,
thanks to Sian.)

831
00:30:19,100 --> 00:30:20,134
You want this one?

832
00:30:20,193 --> 00:30:22,236
Okay. Thank you.

833
00:30:22,237 --> 00:30:23,404
I'm using it right away.

834
00:30:23,940 --> 00:30:25,038
I love it!

835
00:30:25,039 --> 00:30:27,674
(Proud)

836
00:30:27,675 --> 00:30:30,077
This is an amazing item.

837
00:30:30,841 --> 00:30:31,845
Congratulations!

838
00:30:31,846 --> 00:30:33,867
I'm going to be using this in Korea too.

839
00:30:33,868 --> 00:30:35,194
Congratulations.

840
00:30:35,195 --> 00:30:36,417
Thank you!

841
00:30:37,161 --> 00:30:38,685
Wow, that T-shirt is cute.

842
00:30:38,961 --> 00:30:41,121
It kind of looks like a hoodie.

843
00:30:41,167 --> 00:30:42,374
- Should we ask for that?
- Yes.

844
00:30:42,434 --> 00:30:44,333
Hello.

845
00:30:44,347 --> 00:30:45,267
Hello.

846
00:30:46,193 --> 00:30:48,628
- That looks really breezy.
- It's what Gabee would go for.

847
00:30:48,761 --> 00:30:50,030
How much is it?

848
00:30:50,898 --> 00:30:51,832
- For 2.
- It's 500.

849
00:30:51,833 --> 00:30:53,600
Five hundreds?

850
00:30:54,666 --> 00:30:56,040
It's so expensive.

851
00:30:56,041 --> 00:30:56,894
(Shocked)

852
00:30:57,146 --> 00:30:58,098
(Can't give it up.)

853
00:30:58,099 --> 00:30:59,072
I really like it though.

854
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:02,060
Then, make it 350, please.

855
00:31:02,721 --> 00:31:04,032
Make it 350 for 2.

856
00:31:04,033 --> 00:31:05,946
(Negotiation successful)

857
00:31:07,514 --> 00:31:08,715
Then, 300?

858
00:31:10,088 --> 00:31:11,566
- Three hundred?
- Three hundred?

859
00:31:11,567 --> 00:31:13,720
How about 300 baht?

860
00:31:13,721 --> 00:31:16,142
(The 300 choir, chanting)

861
00:31:16,427 --> 00:31:17,528
No. 350.

862
00:31:18,292 --> 00:31:20,060
Then 340.

863
00:31:20,694 --> 00:31:22,654
(Trying again to discount
at least 50 cents)

864
00:31:23,281 --> 00:31:25,554
(Holding firm and saving 50 cents.)

865
00:31:27,137 --> 00:31:29,303
- Okay.
- Oh, 340.

866
00:31:29,583 --> 00:31:31,889
(The ruthless bargain hunter)

867
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,230
Thank you very much!

868
00:31:33,910 --> 00:31:36,903
(Their suitcase is getting filled more.)

869
00:31:37,244 --> 00:31:38,841
You didn't have anything to wear tomorrow.

870
00:31:38,842 --> 00:31:40,280
Yeah, that's right.

871
00:31:40,368 --> 00:31:41,849
- You're wearing that tomorrow, right?
- Sure.

872
00:31:41,850 --> 00:31:42,683
Okay.

873
00:31:42,861 --> 00:31:45,385
Yay, Gabee and I are wearing
the matching shirt tomorrow.

874
00:31:45,595 --> 00:31:46,753
This is so fun.

875
00:31:46,848 --> 00:31:48,589
Haggling is half the fun.

876
00:31:48,590 --> 00:31:49,556
I love it.

877
00:31:50,703 --> 00:31:54,616
Let's pick up our Secret Santa gifts
at the shops outside.

878
00:31:54,723 --> 00:31:56,296
Great idea.

879
00:31:56,597 --> 00:31:58,765
A lot changed
since the last time I visited.

880
00:31:59,462 --> 00:32:01,168
This place is so much fun.

881
00:32:01,989 --> 00:32:04,042
(Posing)

882
00:32:04,378 --> 00:32:06,378
- That's so pretty.
- This place is big.

883
00:32:06,482 --> 00:32:07,474
So pretty.

884
00:32:11,473 --> 00:32:15,440
(Literally "Avatar: The Way of Water")

885
00:32:16,283 --> 00:32:17,718
We made a full loop.

886
00:32:17,753 --> 00:32:19,019
It seems like it.

887
00:32:19,720 --> 00:32:21,154
This is so fun.

888
00:32:21,871 --> 00:32:23,790
I forgot how much fun this place is.

889
00:32:25,292 --> 00:32:26,727
It's so hot.

890
00:32:26,805 --> 00:32:27,861
Is this the end?

891
00:32:28,295 --> 00:32:30,931
I'm so happy we got all we needed.

892
00:32:31,345 --> 00:32:32,866
One person at a time.

893
00:32:32,867 --> 00:32:35,596
(They get off the boat one by one.)

894
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:38,722
(Don't forget the suitcase.)

895
00:32:38,916 --> 00:32:40,240
My pants are all wet.

896
00:32:40,741 --> 00:32:42,741
My pants are wet too.

897
00:32:42,802 --> 00:32:44,156
Harimu's pants are wet too.

898
00:32:44,157 --> 00:32:45,646
I'm sweating all over.

899
00:32:45,689 --> 00:32:47,842
(Twerk-drying)

900
00:32:48,136 --> 00:32:50,316
(Next-level pants drying)

901
00:32:51,276 --> 00:32:52,976
(Turbo dry)

902
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,276
(Mind-blown)

903
00:32:55,422 --> 00:32:57,057
We need to put it in the suitcase.

904
00:32:57,058 --> 00:32:58,358
- Right.
- Yeah, we need to.

905
00:32:58,725 --> 00:33:00,876
I really want to buy an elephant doll.

906
00:33:00,877 --> 00:33:03,730
Then how about we do some
Secret Santa shopping?

907
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:04,736
Gift for Secret Santa?

908
00:33:04,737 --> 00:33:06,852
- Yes, let's do that now.
- Alright. For 10 minutes.

909
00:33:06,853 --> 00:33:08,057
- I'm down.
- Shopping time?

910
00:33:08,058 --> 00:33:09,770
- No peeking.
- Don't look.

911
00:33:09,771 --> 00:33:10,904
Absolutely no peeking.

912
00:33:10,905 --> 00:33:13,034
Don't look at me. I'll get mad.

913
00:33:13,035 --> 00:33:14,408
Stop looking.

914
00:33:14,409 --> 00:33:15,499
(They start secret shopping.)

915
00:33:15,738 --> 00:33:17,092
I'm Secret Santa to...

916
00:33:17,731 --> 00:33:18,879
Gabee.

917
00:33:19,212 --> 00:33:22,816
She told us she likes things
that make noise like instruments.

918
00:33:23,700 --> 00:33:27,321
I saw a rainbow frog
while we were on the boat earlier.

919
00:33:27,322 --> 00:33:28,522
It was so cute.

920
00:33:28,860 --> 00:33:30,991
I couldn't buy it
because she was right next to me.

921
00:33:32,392 --> 00:33:34,127
That frog.

922
00:33:34,531 --> 00:33:36,531
There are not a lot of places
that sell that.

923
00:33:36,930 --> 00:33:39,032
I swear I can hear someone stroking one.

924
00:33:39,299 --> 00:33:40,801
I can hear the croaks.

925
00:33:41,404 --> 00:33:42,551
(Croak)

926
00:33:42,970 --> 00:33:44,458
This could be a good gift too.

927
00:33:45,138 --> 00:33:48,508
You know Hyerim carries
a wooden temple block in her bag, right?

928
00:33:49,376 --> 00:33:51,111
But that obviously doesn't work for her.

929
00:33:51,112 --> 00:33:53,380
Why is she never calm?

930
00:33:54,982 --> 00:33:57,484
Hyerim could use a little calm.

931
00:33:57,666 --> 00:34:02,689
Hyerim told us she needs a mirror earlier.

932
00:34:02,767 --> 00:34:05,492
So, I'll go look for a mirror first.

933
00:34:06,426 --> 00:34:07,794
I should be able to find one.

934
00:34:11,698 --> 00:34:13,033
This thing's awesome.

935
00:34:13,658 --> 00:34:15,377
(Already distracted)

936
00:34:15,378 --> 00:34:16,269
A mask.

937
00:34:16,478 --> 00:34:18,605
This is so cute. I want it for myself.

938
00:34:18,872 --> 00:34:20,045
So cute.

939
00:34:20,046 --> 00:34:21,323
(She's forgotten about the gift too.)

940
00:34:21,899 --> 00:34:22,809
I shouldn't.

941
00:34:23,825 --> 00:34:26,005
(Managed to hold on to her senses.)

942
00:34:26,245 --> 00:34:29,883
Won Ji likes flashy things,
so I'll look for something flashy.

943
00:34:30,306 --> 00:34:31,551
Why is everything so cute?

944
00:34:31,552 --> 00:34:33,186
Won Ji likes things that stand out.

945
00:34:34,618 --> 00:34:35,689
These are all...

946
00:34:35,786 --> 00:34:37,491
Wait a minute. This one is prettier.

947
00:34:38,392 --> 00:34:40,616
(Drawn into the store like a magnet.)

948
00:34:40,617 --> 00:34:41,795
I should've bought this one.

949
00:34:42,396 --> 00:34:44,364
Shouldn't have paid 350.

950
00:34:44,584 --> 00:34:47,000
- It's 150 baht.
- Is this 150?

951
00:34:47,210 --> 00:34:48,210
Really?

952
00:34:48,211 --> 00:34:49,870
She says it's 150.

953
00:34:50,470 --> 00:34:52,039
I paid 350 earlier.

954
00:34:52,692 --> 00:34:53,840
Okay.

955
00:34:53,841 --> 00:34:56,408
(She bought it as Won Ji's gift.)

956
00:34:56,409 --> 00:34:59,513
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

957
00:34:59,980 --> 00:35:03,050
Won Ji needs a bit of color.

958
00:35:03,750 --> 00:35:04,818
Here we go.

959
00:35:04,819 --> 00:35:06,286
(I found my color.)

960
00:35:06,299 --> 00:35:07,220
Hello.

961
00:35:07,279 --> 00:35:08,255
Big size.

962
00:35:08,653 --> 00:35:09,723
Big size.

963
00:35:09,853 --> 00:35:12,192
Not for me, for my friend.

964
00:35:12,553 --> 00:35:13,593
Big size.

965
00:35:14,150 --> 00:35:15,529
Or this one.

966
00:35:16,630 --> 00:35:17,998
No bigger size?

967
00:35:18,932 --> 00:35:20,600
This is too small for Won Ji.

968
00:35:22,324 --> 00:35:24,229
(Stretch)

969
00:35:24,237 --> 00:35:25,408
(What do you think?)

970
00:35:26,488 --> 00:35:26,942
(Hmm)

971
00:35:27,268 --> 00:35:27,608
(Flip)

972
00:35:30,108 --> 00:35:31,928
(Still a no?)

973
00:35:32,828 --> 00:35:33,648
(Hmm)

974
00:35:33,668 --> 00:35:34,347
Big.

975
00:35:34,348 --> 00:35:35,662
(That thing won't fit on her.)

976
00:35:35,941 --> 00:35:36,843
(Bigger?)

977
00:35:36,888 --> 00:35:38,552
I think this would be too small.

978
00:35:39,286 --> 00:35:40,787
Too small.

979
00:35:40,942 --> 00:35:42,823
But it's so pretty.

980
00:35:43,390 --> 00:35:45,292
- How much is it?
- That's 300 baht.

981
00:35:47,294 --> 00:35:50,163
(That's too expensive.)

982
00:35:50,509 --> 00:35:52,063
What about 150 baht?

983
00:35:53,777 --> 00:35:56,269
(It's too small.)

984
00:35:56,390 --> 00:35:58,437
(The small size, half the price.)

985
00:35:58,438 --> 00:35:59,936
(Hmm)

986
00:35:59,937 --> 00:36:01,475
It might be a little small.

987
00:36:01,476 --> 00:36:02,843
It's too big!

988
00:36:03,343 --> 00:36:05,679
This is too big. I need a smaller size.

989
00:36:06,873 --> 00:36:10,550
We need a smaller one
because we need to carry it back.

990
00:36:10,588 --> 00:36:11,384
Huh?

991
00:36:11,581 --> 00:36:12,853
You weren't following me, were you?

992
00:36:14,588 --> 00:36:16,022
Pretending you didn't see me, huh?

993
00:36:16,115 --> 00:36:17,190
Frog.

994
00:36:17,891 --> 00:36:19,593
That one was way too big.

995
00:36:19,788 --> 00:36:21,895
That frog was too big. 175.

996
00:36:21,921 --> 00:36:23,997
We keep bumping into each other.

997
00:36:24,414 --> 00:36:25,380
(Unidentified?)

998
00:36:25,381 --> 00:36:26,633
We keep bumping into each other.

999
00:36:27,027 --> 00:36:29,347
(Hiding behind the couple's hat.)

1000
00:36:29,574 --> 00:36:32,873
Sian seems to really love elephants.

1001
00:36:33,060 --> 00:36:37,271
I should buy her a bunch
of elephant-related things.

1002
00:36:37,458 --> 00:36:39,813
Elephant-themed collection.

1003
00:36:40,747 --> 00:36:43,350
She wanted an elephant doll too.

1004
00:36:44,885 --> 00:36:46,086
This one's pretty. It's pink.

1005
00:36:47,216 --> 00:36:48,155
(Color?)

1006
00:36:48,270 --> 00:36:49,122
Pink one.

1007
00:36:49,422 --> 00:36:52,163
I want pink.

1008
00:36:52,563 --> 00:36:54,027
Wait, I need to hide these, though.

1009
00:36:55,390 --> 00:36:56,156
Gosh!

1010
00:36:56,930 --> 00:36:58,532
How do I even hide this?

1011
00:36:59,065 --> 00:37:00,801
What if she already bought one?

1012
00:37:02,068 --> 00:37:04,471
I want this.

1013
00:37:05,348 --> 00:37:06,506
Thank you.

1014
00:37:07,261 --> 00:37:09,312
(She already bought a mint elephant.)

1015
00:37:09,805 --> 00:37:11,311
I just keep adopting elephants.

1016
00:37:11,745 --> 00:37:13,246
That's enough, Sian.

1017
00:37:13,613 --> 00:37:14,648
What's this?

1018
00:37:15,048 --> 00:37:17,317
This is really cute, isn't it?

1019
00:37:17,717 --> 00:37:19,219
You can hang it...

1020
00:37:19,459 --> 00:37:21,288
and use it for something, right?

1021
00:37:21,721 --> 00:37:22,797
This one's pretty.

1022
00:37:22,877 --> 00:37:23,824
How much is this?

1023
00:37:24,089 --> 00:37:25,416
- That's 300 baht.
- What?

1024
00:37:27,160 --> 00:37:28,094
What?

1025
00:37:28,317 --> 00:37:29,362
Did you say 300?

1026
00:37:31,177 --> 00:37:33,501
(Let the haggling begin.)

1027
00:37:33,502 --> 00:37:34,801
Make it 150.

1028
00:37:35,335 --> 00:37:36,503
What about 200?

1029
00:37:36,514 --> 00:37:37,261
(Shaking)

1030
00:37:37,295 --> 00:37:39,015
(Stop me.)

1031
00:37:39,868 --> 00:37:41,041
Did you see that?

1032
00:37:41,048 --> 00:37:42,375
This is how you push and pull.

1033
00:37:42,481 --> 00:37:44,778
You have to act like you can't fight it.

1034
00:37:44,779 --> 00:37:46,272
That's how it works.

1035
00:37:47,206 --> 00:37:48,546
My gift for Hyerim.

1036
00:37:49,216 --> 00:37:51,084
I love things like these.

1037
00:37:52,018 --> 00:37:54,187
I've never seen anything like it.

1038
00:37:54,588 --> 00:37:56,089
I'm going to go there and check out bags.

1039
00:37:57,650 --> 00:37:59,159
This is a bag paradise.

1040
00:38:00,560 --> 00:38:02,095
I want this.

1041
00:38:03,020 --> 00:38:04,059
(She suddenly is possessed by a cat.)

1042
00:38:04,060 --> 00:38:06,066
It's so cute. How much is it?

1043
00:38:07,677 --> 00:38:08,935
Is this 200 baht?

1044
00:38:08,957 --> 00:38:10,403
No.

1045
00:38:10,484 --> 00:38:13,473
Please give me a discount.

1046
00:38:13,474 --> 00:38:16,276
Please give me a discount.

1047
00:38:16,930 --> 00:38:18,879
Please give it to me for 150.

1048
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,280
Meow.

1049
00:38:20,281 --> 00:38:21,948
- Okay.
- Meow!

1050
00:38:22,553 --> 00:38:26,586
(I made this 2.5 dollars cheaper!)

1051
00:38:26,860 --> 00:38:27,953
(While she's on a roll...)

1052
00:38:28,006 --> 00:38:29,322
(1, 3, 0.)

1053
00:38:29,589 --> 00:38:31,555
One hundred thirty.

1054
00:38:31,556 --> 00:38:33,326
(Not a chance!)

1055
00:38:34,060 --> 00:38:35,762
Then 140, please!

1056
00:38:35,886 --> 00:38:37,692
(The ultimate price showdown.)

1057
00:38:37,693 --> 00:38:39,033
How much is this?

1058
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:40,267
It's 120 baht.

1059
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:42,406
Oh, come on. 100.

1060
00:38:43,036 --> 00:38:44,768
(But that shop offered...)

1061
00:38:44,769 --> 00:38:46,817
- Okay!
- For 100?

1062
00:38:46,818 --> 00:38:48,642
(Deal struck at 100 baht.)

1063
00:38:49,142 --> 00:38:50,410
Oh, no.

1064
00:38:50,857 --> 00:38:52,579
We can't air this.

1065
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:53,580
(Not-for-TV Zone)

1066
00:38:53,682 --> 00:38:55,450
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1067
00:38:55,451 --> 00:38:58,188
(Won Ji bought a gift for Gabee.)

1068
00:38:58,668 --> 00:39:00,221
Awesome.

1069
00:39:00,687 --> 00:39:01,721
I'll hide it.

1070
00:39:03,123 --> 00:39:04,658
Am I the first to return?

1071
00:39:06,026 --> 00:39:08,461
You bought yours?

1072
00:39:08,694 --> 00:39:11,131
- Looks like you have it in there.
- I'm busted!

1073
00:39:11,201 --> 00:39:12,565
Don't look!

1074
00:39:12,999 --> 00:39:14,367
Yours seems pretty big.

1075
00:39:14,468 --> 00:39:16,536
She's back. She bought a lot.

1076
00:39:16,841 --> 00:39:19,873
I need way more time.
I want to keep shopping.

1077
00:39:19,994 --> 00:39:21,734
Then, how about we...

1078
00:39:21,735 --> 00:39:25,111
reveal these later at the hotel?

1079
00:39:25,168 --> 00:39:27,101
- Let's put it in the suitcase for now.
- Okay.

1080
00:39:27,307 --> 00:39:28,882
Opening suitcase.

1081
00:39:29,349 --> 00:39:30,884
Open.

1082
00:39:31,049 --> 00:39:31,969
Okay!

1083
00:39:31,970 --> 00:39:33,620
Can you all close your eyes, please?

1084
00:39:33,669 --> 00:39:34,955
Close your eyes.

1085
00:39:35,062 --> 00:39:36,289
Done!

1086
00:39:36,623 --> 00:39:37,757
Mine's in.

1087
00:39:37,876 --> 00:39:40,093
Close your eyes, everyone.

1088
00:39:40,727 --> 00:39:42,929
Keep them closed for a while.
I have a lot to put in.

1089
00:39:43,463 --> 00:39:46,399
Close your eyes, please.

1090
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:49,422
(They are closed.)

1091
00:39:49,576 --> 00:39:51,037
I think I'm done.

1092
00:39:51,780 --> 00:39:53,514
(Suitcase is packed with gifts
for Secret Santa.)

1093
00:39:53,680 --> 00:39:55,460
- Let's go!
- I'm so happy.

1094
00:39:55,520 --> 00:39:56,759
Yes, let's go.

1095
00:39:56,760 --> 00:39:58,645
(Moving to the next destination)

1096
00:39:59,655 --> 00:40:01,491
We got in the car.

1097
00:40:02,782 --> 00:40:04,549
We're heading there now.

1098
00:40:04,817 --> 00:40:06,085
We're going to the cave.

1099
00:40:06,086 --> 00:40:06,952
(Excited)

1100
00:40:06,953 --> 00:40:08,921
- We're going to the cave.
- Cave!

1101
00:40:09,155 --> 00:40:10,555
Phraya Nakhon Cave.

1102
00:40:10,556 --> 00:40:11,523
(Searching)

1103
00:40:11,524 --> 00:40:12,725
Phraya Nakhon Cave.

1104
00:40:12,860 --> 00:40:15,093
Have any of you ever been to a cave?

1105
00:40:15,094 --> 00:40:16,562
When you travel,

1106
00:40:16,696 --> 00:40:19,497
is anyone here the type
who likes going into nature?

1107
00:40:22,402 --> 00:40:24,336
A cave is the ultimate nature experience.

1108
00:40:24,471 --> 00:40:27,439
And apparently, sunlight shines into it.

1109
00:40:28,391 --> 00:40:29,741
Because there's an opening...

1110
00:40:29,742 --> 00:40:30,575
(Looks away)

1111
00:40:30,576 --> 00:40:31,776
Bitch cave...

1112
00:40:31,777 --> 00:40:33,712
(Fails to resist)

1113
00:40:34,013 --> 00:40:37,716
(Won Ji can't get used
to their mindless reactions)

1114
00:40:37,717 --> 00:40:39,818
We can never have a proper conversation.

1115
00:40:39,819 --> 00:40:42,020
We can't have a proper conversation.

1116
00:40:42,789 --> 00:40:44,390
Let's go to the cave.

1117
00:40:44,391 --> 00:40:45,357
(See you soon, cave.)

1118
00:40:45,358 --> 00:40:46,925
Guys.

1119
00:40:46,926 --> 00:40:48,827
They said that once we buy the tickets,

1120
00:40:48,828 --> 00:40:50,662
we have to start trekking right away.

1121
00:40:52,565 --> 00:40:55,100
The trail isn't flat,
so they recommend wearing sneakers.

1122
00:40:55,107 --> 00:40:56,726
We have to walk?

1123
00:40:56,970 --> 00:40:57,802
Yes, we do.

1124
00:40:58,004 --> 00:40:59,304
- Oh, no.
- A lot.

1125
00:40:59,539 --> 00:41:01,206
- A lot?
- It's a trek.

1126
00:41:01,541 --> 00:41:02,374
But it's a cave?

1127
00:41:02,809 --> 00:41:05,445
I guess we have to climb quite a bit
even though it's a cave.

1128
00:41:05,446 --> 00:41:06,779
This isn't what I had in mind.

1129
00:41:06,780 --> 00:41:09,381
Exactly, I was picturing
a cool, refreshing cave.

1130
00:41:09,849 --> 00:41:11,550
Apparently, there's also a beach nearby.

1131
00:41:12,719 --> 00:41:15,320
If we take a boat,
it takes about 20 minutes.

1132
00:41:15,321 --> 00:41:18,690
If we don't, we have to walk
about 2 kilometers.

1133
00:41:18,725 --> 00:41:20,325
Should we take the boat?

1134
00:41:20,326 --> 00:41:21,760
Of course.

1135
00:41:21,828 --> 00:41:24,496
Let's take the boat.

1136
00:41:24,497 --> 00:41:26,598
We don't have time to hike
all the way there.

1137
00:41:26,599 --> 00:41:27,766
That's true.

1138
00:41:28,768 --> 00:41:29,601
Oh, my.

1139
00:41:29,969 --> 00:41:32,270
The new aespa song, "Lemonade," came out.

1140
00:41:32,271 --> 00:41:33,105
I know.

1141
00:41:33,239 --> 00:41:34,806
The choreography we created is in it.

1142
00:41:34,807 --> 00:41:36,207
- Really?
- Really?

1143
00:41:36,232 --> 00:41:37,775
(Happy news arrives during the trip.)

1144
00:41:37,776 --> 00:41:39,377
I'm curious.
Did the song come out already?

1145
00:41:39,378 --> 00:41:40,578
Yes, it's out now.

1146
00:41:40,814 --> 00:41:41,914
The signature move is by La Chica.

1147
00:41:42,115 --> 00:41:43,615
The signature move is everything.

1148
00:41:43,750 --> 00:41:46,351
La Chica is really good
at creating iconic choreography.

1149
00:41:46,553 --> 00:41:47,886
I think we're a great match with aespa.

1150
00:41:48,655 --> 00:41:50,823
How old were you when you started dancing?

1151
00:41:50,824 --> 00:41:51,724
Ten.

1152
00:41:52,325 --> 00:41:54,060
But I was dancing even before that.

1153
00:41:54,061 --> 00:41:55,227
Just by myself at home.

1154
00:41:55,662 --> 00:41:56,862
Harimu, what about you?

1155
00:41:57,030 --> 00:42:00,032
Me too. I started taking
dance classes in elementary school.

1156
00:42:00,033 --> 00:42:01,166
(Elementary school Harimu)

1157
00:42:01,267 --> 00:42:03,201
She was really good even back then.

1158
00:42:03,370 --> 00:42:04,770
I remember her.

1159
00:42:04,771 --> 00:42:06,371
You went to the School
of Performing Arts Seoul, right?

1160
00:42:06,506 --> 00:42:07,306
Yes, I did.

1161
00:42:07,874 --> 00:42:09,442
I took a lot of Gabee's classes.

1162
00:42:09,443 --> 00:42:11,310
Was she your student?

1163
00:42:11,311 --> 00:42:12,978
She'd drop into my classes
from time to time.

1164
00:42:12,979 --> 00:42:14,479
She was one of the talented kids.

1165
00:42:14,614 --> 00:42:16,515
- That's cool.
- You could tell at a glance.

1166
00:42:16,516 --> 00:42:17,983
She's the kind of person you remember.

1167
00:42:17,984 --> 00:42:19,084
I agree.

1168
00:42:19,085 --> 00:42:20,752
I think it's great to have
distinctive character.

1169
00:42:20,753 --> 00:42:21,553
Right.

1170
00:42:21,554 --> 00:42:23,055
There are people who catch your attention.

1171
00:42:23,056 --> 00:42:25,490
- That's true.
- I think star quality is important.

1172
00:42:25,491 --> 00:42:27,326
Exactly. That's what amazes me.

1173
00:42:27,327 --> 00:42:29,728
This is so interesting.
I know nothing about this world.

1174
00:42:30,697 --> 00:42:32,464
I want to learn dancing from Gabee too.

1175
00:42:32,465 --> 00:42:34,433
La Chica is totally my style.

1176
00:42:35,568 --> 00:42:37,035
I seriously loved La Chica.

1177
00:42:37,036 --> 00:42:38,336
Can I even say this?

1178
00:42:38,705 --> 00:42:41,774
When "Street Woman Fighter" was airing,

1179
00:42:42,141 --> 00:42:45,044
I loved La Chica so much,
and I was a huge fan of Gabee.

1180
00:42:45,045 --> 00:42:48,546
I loved her so much that,

1181
00:42:48,981 --> 00:42:50,916
for the first and only time in my life,

1182
00:42:51,050 --> 00:42:52,284
I sent you a DM.

1183
00:42:52,285 --> 00:42:53,986
You said so, but I had no idea.

1184
00:42:54,587 --> 00:42:56,421
- I wonder if it's still there.
- Oh, no.

1185
00:42:56,422 --> 00:42:57,788
Let's see what she wrote.

1186
00:42:57,789 --> 00:43:00,559
(Dopamine is skyrocketing.)

1187
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:03,295
It was something like,
"I'm such a huge fan. I love you."

1188
00:43:03,363 --> 00:43:05,198
I was 22 then,

1189
00:43:05,199 --> 00:43:06,765
so about five years ago.

1190
00:43:06,766 --> 00:43:08,434
Has it already been five years?

1191
00:43:08,435 --> 00:43:09,401
(She suddenly starts talking a lot.)

1192
00:43:09,769 --> 00:43:11,287
- It's still here.
- Really?

1193
00:43:11,312 --> 00:43:13,347
"Gabee, I love you. I'm such a huge fan."

1194
00:43:13,372 --> 00:43:15,540
"Everyone around me knows
how much I like you."

1195
00:43:15,541 --> 00:43:17,175
"I've never sent a DM like this before."

1196
00:43:17,176 --> 00:43:19,444
"I watch 'Street Woman Fighter'
every time because of you."

1197
00:43:19,445 --> 00:43:22,448
"I always support you, I love you."
She sent this in 2021.

1198
00:43:22,449 --> 00:43:24,317
See, Gabee? I told you I was serious.

1199
00:43:24,318 --> 00:43:25,418
I guess you did.

1200
00:43:25,419 --> 00:43:27,886
- But you didn't show it at all.
- I should finally reply.

1201
00:43:27,887 --> 00:43:30,088
Thank you, Sian.

1202
00:43:30,089 --> 00:43:31,623
(Thank you, Sian.)

1203
00:43:31,624 --> 00:43:32,424
After all these years...

1204
00:43:32,425 --> 00:43:35,460
If you really admire someone,
you eventually end up meeting them.

1205
00:43:36,863 --> 00:43:39,731
So I'm getting a reply after five years?

1206
00:43:39,732 --> 00:43:43,368
Now I understand why people send DMs...

1207
00:43:43,369 --> 00:43:46,171
to celebrities or people they admire.

1208
00:43:46,172 --> 00:43:48,474
Sending a DM really takes courage.

1209
00:43:48,574 --> 00:43:50,431
I'm not the type to send DMs
to just anyone.

1210
00:43:50,432 --> 00:43:53,278
(Wishing the two of them
a beautiful friendship)

1211
00:43:53,479 --> 00:43:55,046
I'm truly a successful fan.

1212
00:43:55,047 --> 00:43:56,881
You're truly a successful fan.

1213
00:43:57,083 --> 00:43:58,984
When they first told you...

1214
00:43:58,985 --> 00:44:01,286
we'd be traveling with just one suitcase,

1215
00:44:01,287 --> 00:44:03,255
you must have thought it'd be hard.

1216
00:44:03,256 --> 00:44:05,290
So why did you agree to it?

1217
00:44:05,425 --> 00:44:06,625
For me...

1218
00:44:08,995 --> 00:44:11,364
I just heard we were going on a trip,
so I said yes.

1219
00:44:13,433 --> 00:44:15,401
You just wanted to get away.

1220
00:44:15,701 --> 00:44:18,469
The production staff
talked about the suitcase,

1221
00:44:18,470 --> 00:44:20,304
but I wasn't really listening.

1222
00:44:20,706 --> 00:44:21,539
What about you, Harimu?

1223
00:44:22,175 --> 00:44:24,443
Why did you accept it?

1224
00:44:24,444 --> 00:44:26,111
For me...

1225
00:44:26,112 --> 00:44:29,915
whenever I travel, I always end up
buying things to bring home.

1226
00:44:30,150 --> 00:44:35,020
I think I wanted to change that habit.

1227
00:44:35,021 --> 00:44:38,190
- You came to that conclusion quite early.
- Absolutely.

1228
00:44:38,191 --> 00:44:39,658
I'm still not very good at it.

1229
00:44:39,659 --> 00:44:40,592
(I'm still figuring things out)

1230
00:44:40,593 --> 00:44:43,328
Maybe it's about time I started trying.

1231
00:44:43,329 --> 00:44:44,396
(The youngest is one step ahead.)

1232
00:44:44,397 --> 00:44:46,164
As my personal taste became more defined,

1233
00:44:46,566 --> 00:44:49,268
I started becoming
obsessed with certain items.

1234
00:44:49,502 --> 00:44:51,770
- Glasses...
- Glasses, hats.

1235
00:44:51,771 --> 00:44:53,638
I like silver rings too.

1236
00:44:53,873 --> 00:44:56,874
I should buy a silver ring
while I'm in Thailand.

1237
00:44:56,875 --> 00:44:57,776
Right.

1238
00:44:58,578 --> 00:45:00,144
Just thinking about it makes me mad.

1239
00:45:00,213 --> 00:45:01,213
Mad?

1240
00:45:01,514 --> 00:45:02,481
I'm mad.

1241
00:45:02,482 --> 00:45:04,649
So instead of "Abra-ca-Empty,"

1242
00:45:04,750 --> 00:45:05,684
Something else?

1243
00:45:05,685 --> 00:45:07,285
We go with an empty suitcase,

1244
00:45:07,286 --> 00:45:08,319
and filling it up.

1245
00:45:08,320 --> 00:45:09,387
"Abra-ca-Fill."

1246
00:45:10,089 --> 00:45:12,390
(That's actually pretty good.
Why don't people do that?)

1247
00:45:12,892 --> 00:45:14,226
"Abra-ca-Load."

1248
00:45:14,961 --> 00:45:17,229
I love that.
I'm seriously confident about that.

1249
00:45:17,230 --> 00:45:18,764
Me too.

1250
00:45:18,831 --> 00:45:20,365
Do you think we'll become minimalists,

1251
00:45:20,933 --> 00:45:22,467
by the end of this trip?

1252
00:45:23,069 --> 00:45:24,903
But is becoming a minimalist
even our dream?

1253
00:45:24,904 --> 00:45:26,937
Why do we have to become minimalists?

1254
00:45:26,938 --> 00:45:30,108
Still, it's important to experience
minimalist travel.

1255
00:45:30,476 --> 00:45:31,810
That way, you get to know yourself better.

1256
00:45:31,811 --> 00:45:32,977
Absolutely.

1257
00:45:32,978 --> 00:45:34,379
It's a process of getting to know myself.

1258
00:45:34,380 --> 00:45:35,980
You figure out
what's truly important to you.

1259
00:45:35,981 --> 00:45:37,782
(They quickly try to recover.)

1260
00:45:37,884 --> 00:45:39,451
(Thinking)

1261
00:45:39,452 --> 00:45:42,988
Whenever I traveled before,
my friends and I were...

1262
00:45:42,989 --> 00:45:45,324
always busy taking pictures.

1263
00:45:45,325 --> 00:45:47,593
I always traveled...

1264
00:45:48,027 --> 00:45:50,595
looking perfectly put together.

1265
00:45:50,596 --> 00:45:54,566
I traveled mainly
so I could post on social media.

1266
00:45:55,202 --> 00:45:58,037
- Eventually, I realized I hated that.
- I see.

1267
00:45:58,038 --> 00:46:00,639
But when she travels,

1268
00:46:00,640 --> 00:46:02,407
she creates beautiful content.

1269
00:46:02,408 --> 00:46:04,576
She does her makeup, and she dresses up.

1270
00:46:04,577 --> 00:46:06,245
- That means she has so much to pack.
- I know.

1271
00:46:06,246 --> 00:46:09,552
Honestly, travel starts to feel like work.

1272
00:46:09,553 --> 00:46:11,116
- It's more like for filming.
- Exactly.

1273
00:46:11,117 --> 00:46:13,619
There's this pressure
to create great content,

1274
00:46:13,620 --> 00:46:15,787
so I never really
got to enjoy the trip itself.

1275
00:46:15,788 --> 00:46:16,822
I see.

1276
00:46:16,823 --> 00:46:19,291
But if I do it this way,

1277
00:46:19,592 --> 00:46:21,660
maybe I can focus entirely on the trip,

1278
00:46:21,661 --> 00:46:23,261
and genuinely enjoy it.

1279
00:46:23,529 --> 00:46:27,165
Actually, traveling with such a small
suitcase isn't bad at all.

1280
00:46:27,166 --> 00:46:28,933
Also, it's kind of fun.

1281
00:46:28,934 --> 00:46:30,568
It's fun buying what you need locally.

1282
00:46:30,569 --> 00:46:32,937
- And moving around is so much easier.
- Absolutely.

1283
00:46:33,106 --> 00:46:36,608
I think we'll appreciate it even more
as the trip goes on.

1284
00:46:36,976 --> 00:46:39,678
I don't have to worry about choosing
an outfit every morning.

1285
00:46:39,679 --> 00:46:41,413
I don't have to worry about makeup.

1286
00:46:41,414 --> 00:46:44,483
And the four of us have a similar level
of interest in dressing up.

1287
00:46:44,508 --> 00:46:45,654
- Indeed.
- I like that.

1288
00:46:45,784 --> 00:46:47,419
We gave up pretty early.

1289
00:46:47,420 --> 00:46:48,887
Even quicker than I thought you would.

1290
00:46:48,888 --> 00:46:51,356
- So we can sleep more now!
- I love that too.

1291
00:46:51,457 --> 00:46:54,626
I thought I'd gradually stop caring,

1292
00:46:55,061 --> 00:46:57,429
but I basically went
full survival mode from day one.

1293
00:46:57,897 --> 00:46:58,930
Go savage.

1294
00:46:58,931 --> 00:47:01,399
It feels like the quality of the trip
has improved.

1295
00:47:01,834 --> 00:47:02,802
It feels like a real trip.

1296
00:47:03,269 --> 00:47:05,704
They said it's a two-hour drive.

1297
00:47:05,705 --> 00:47:08,440
Actually, between 2 and 2.5 hours.

1298
00:47:08,608 --> 00:47:09,875
Everyone, get some sleep.

1299
00:47:11,878 --> 00:47:18,250
(As they continued
driving along the road,)

1300
00:47:18,251 --> 00:47:21,453
(their destination gradually drew closer.)

1301
00:47:21,921 --> 00:47:23,955
The scenery has changed.

1302
00:47:23,956 --> 00:47:24,956
(Looking around)

1303
00:47:28,394 --> 00:47:30,695
I've never been
somewhere like this before.

1304
00:47:34,567 --> 00:47:35,967
This place is really beautiful.

1305
00:47:36,702 --> 00:47:37,635
Are those rice fields?

1306
00:47:40,073 --> 00:47:42,173
Those are limestone cliffs.

1307
00:47:43,075 --> 00:47:43,941
Rocky mountains.

1308
00:47:45,044 --> 00:47:47,712
Those are all rocky mountains.

1309
00:47:48,714 --> 00:47:50,014
This place looks amazing.

1310
00:47:50,015 --> 00:47:51,381
(The rocky mountains
surrounding Phraya Nakhon Cave)

1311
00:47:51,382 --> 00:47:53,651
I had no idea Thailand was this vast.

1312
00:47:53,886 --> 00:47:56,254
It feels like the land
just goes on forever.

1313
00:47:59,158 --> 00:48:00,892
We've come to the countryside.

1314
00:48:00,893 --> 00:48:02,460
This is real countryside.

1315
00:48:04,163 --> 00:48:05,296
Yes, it's real countryside.

1316
00:48:06,132 --> 00:48:07,432
(They spot the sign.)

1317
00:48:07,433 --> 00:48:08,667
I think we're here.

1318
00:48:11,260 --> 00:48:13,371
Look, the boat.
The beach is right in front of us.

1319
00:48:13,372 --> 00:48:15,807
The beach is right there.

1320
00:48:15,832 --> 00:48:18,927
(The entrance to Phraya Nakhon Cave
sits right beside the sea.)

1321
00:48:19,046 --> 00:48:20,378
There's the beach.

1322
00:48:20,379 --> 00:48:21,346
(Excited)

1323
00:48:22,515 --> 00:48:23,715
Are we getting out?

1324
00:48:23,716 --> 00:48:25,116
Don't forget your phone.

1325
00:48:27,920 --> 00:48:31,789
(They finally get out
after a 2.5-hour drive at 2:30 p.m.)

1326
00:48:35,194 --> 00:48:36,027
It's hot.

1327
00:48:37,063 --> 00:48:38,264
Change into your sneakers.

1328
00:48:38,265 --> 00:48:41,333
(They don't forget
to switch into walking shoes.)

1329
00:48:41,500 --> 00:48:43,267
There are lots of stray dogs here.

1330
00:48:45,638 --> 00:48:46,871
Stray dogs.

1331
00:48:48,541 --> 00:48:50,075
They just wander around.

1332
00:48:50,643 --> 00:48:51,509
Hello.

1333
00:48:52,978 --> 00:48:54,078
Let's go.

1334
00:48:54,413 --> 00:48:56,914
- I think we can go that way.
- There's Mr. Golden Crab.

1335
00:48:57,883 --> 00:48:59,016
There's a dragon.

1336
00:48:59,017 --> 00:48:59,851
(Flashy)

1337
00:49:00,152 --> 00:49:02,220
It's kind of scary. What is it?

1338
00:49:02,822 --> 00:49:04,656
It's a crab. Why is it there?

1339
00:49:04,657 --> 00:49:05,791
(Strikes a pose immediately)

1340
00:49:06,125 --> 00:49:07,625
(Cute)

1341
00:49:08,060 --> 00:49:10,061
(A dance dedicated to Mr. Golden Crab)

1342
00:49:10,062 --> 00:49:11,863
A good sleep really
brought you back to life.

1343
00:49:12,532 --> 00:49:14,131
Is the dog coming with us?

1344
00:49:14,834 --> 00:49:15,733
Maybe it's going to guide us.

1345
00:49:15,734 --> 00:49:17,702
- I think so.
- Are you guiding us?

1346
00:49:19,005 --> 00:49:19,904
(Follow me.)

1347
00:49:19,905 --> 00:49:20,772
Follow me.

1348
00:49:21,040 --> 00:49:24,843
- They said there's an entrance fee.
- Right, it's 200 baht per person.

1349
00:49:25,177 --> 00:49:28,279
- Is this where we go up?
- It's here.

1350
00:49:29,348 --> 00:49:30,514
(They find the ticket booth.)

1351
00:49:30,515 --> 00:49:31,582
Let's see. How much is it?

1352
00:49:34,021 --> 00:49:36,154
- They only take cash.
- It's 200 baht.

1353
00:49:36,155 --> 00:49:37,889
It's quite expensive.

1354
00:49:39,384 --> 00:49:41,959
- Hello there.
- Hello.

1355
00:49:41,960 --> 00:49:44,530
It's 800 baht in total, right?

1356
00:49:45,831 --> 00:49:47,164
Our treasurer.

1357
00:49:48,367 --> 00:49:51,569
(The treasurer hands out the tickets.)

1358
00:49:52,772 --> 00:49:53,605
Look at the sea.

1359
00:49:54,273 --> 00:49:55,139
The sea.

1360
00:49:57,309 --> 00:50:00,278
Hold on, it says 2 kilometers over there.

1361
00:50:00,634 --> 00:50:01,981
Is this real?

1362
00:50:01,982 --> 00:50:03,316
It is real.

1363
00:50:03,495 --> 00:50:06,185
Wait. Do we really have to climb this?

1364
00:50:06,186 --> 00:50:07,520
For real? Those are stone steps.

1365
00:50:07,521 --> 00:50:09,548
(The stone steps look endless.)

1366
00:50:09,549 --> 00:50:11,662
Let's go.
If it gets too tiring, we can turn back.

1367
00:50:11,663 --> 00:50:13,759
I like stopping halfway.

1368
00:50:13,914 --> 00:50:15,661
I never stop halfway.

1369
00:50:15,768 --> 00:50:17,196
You'd rather quit before you even try?

1370
00:50:17,261 --> 00:50:17,964
Yes.

1371
00:50:19,290 --> 00:50:22,290
Didn't it say we'd take a boat?

1372
00:50:22,315 --> 00:50:23,636
Right. They said we could take a boat.

1373
00:50:23,637 --> 00:50:25,115
- Right.
- Even though it's expensive.

1374
00:50:25,455 --> 00:50:27,640
- A boat...
- Where do we take it?

1375
00:50:28,007 --> 00:50:29,375
- Really?
- They said there'd be a boat.

1376
00:50:29,376 --> 00:50:30,610
That's the ocean.

1377
00:50:30,795 --> 00:50:31,844
"Boat to..."

1378
00:50:34,155 --> 00:50:36,115
It was right next to us.

1379
00:50:36,282 --> 00:50:38,929
(You can take the boat here.)

1380
00:50:39,875 --> 00:50:41,253
Can we take a boat?

1381
00:50:41,254 --> 00:50:43,249
(Nodding)

1382
00:50:43,315 --> 00:50:44,557
How much is it?

1383
00:50:44,809 --> 00:50:45,715
Free?

1384
00:50:45,962 --> 00:50:47,059
It's 400 baht.

1385
00:50:47,875 --> 00:50:49,489
(It's more expensive than they thought.)

1386
00:50:49,702 --> 00:50:50,722
For a round trip.

1387
00:50:50,995 --> 00:50:52,435
It's a round trip.

1388
00:50:52,489 --> 00:50:55,029
It covers both trips!

1389
00:50:55,030 --> 00:50:57,136
Okay. Let's go.

1390
00:50:57,189 --> 00:50:58,204
Let's go.

1391
00:50:58,954 --> 00:50:59,839
Tickets?

1392
00:50:59,840 --> 00:51:02,720
(They hand over their tickets.)

1393
00:51:03,194 --> 00:51:04,744
They clip them together.

1394
00:51:05,254 --> 00:51:07,513
That's kind of analog.

1395
00:51:08,180 --> 00:51:09,682
- Number nine?
- Nine.

1396
00:51:11,114 --> 00:51:15,167
(Boat fare: 400 baht,
budget left: 2,472 baht)

1397
00:51:15,168 --> 00:51:17,356
- The boat!
- Let's go.

1398
00:51:17,357 --> 00:51:19,158
We're going to take a boat!

1399
00:51:19,159 --> 00:51:21,837
(Finally, they leave to take a boat.)

1400
00:51:21,891 --> 00:51:23,429
- Let's go!
- Okay.

1401
00:51:23,430 --> 00:51:24,630
Get your energy up!

1402
00:51:25,655 --> 00:51:27,561
(Get your energy up!)

1403
00:51:27,996 --> 00:51:30,150
(Hyping themselves up before leaving)

1404
00:51:30,151 --> 00:51:31,671
Bring your energy!

1405
00:51:32,189 --> 00:51:33,485
(Meowing)

1406
00:51:34,730 --> 00:51:35,908
Let's go.

1407
00:51:37,056 --> 00:51:39,478
It says "cave."

1408
00:51:39,628 --> 00:51:41,747
"Phraya Nakhon Cave."

1409
00:51:41,748 --> 00:51:43,616
That's our destination.

1410
00:51:43,654 --> 00:51:47,553
The thing inside there is called
a pavilion.

1411
00:51:47,648 --> 00:51:49,989
The view here was so beautiful...

1412
00:51:50,054 --> 00:51:52,458
that the royal family built a pavilion.

1413
00:51:52,781 --> 00:51:54,306
Really?

1414
00:51:54,307 --> 00:51:56,462
You can even see this place on postcards.

1415
00:51:56,463 --> 00:51:57,296
Right.

1416
00:51:57,297 --> 00:52:00,900
Everything I see looks so cool.

1417
00:52:00,901 --> 00:52:03,602
(Meowing)

1418
00:52:03,603 --> 00:52:07,150
This place is full of pristine nature.

1419
00:52:07,151 --> 00:52:09,542
- It's impressive.
- Even the sand feels different.

1420
00:52:09,543 --> 00:52:11,724
It's like stepping back
to the very beginning of Earth.

1421
00:52:12,438 --> 00:52:14,714
The very beginning of Earth?
Then we're dinosaurs.

1422
00:52:15,381 --> 00:52:16,916
Hi. How are you?

1423
00:52:16,917 --> 00:52:19,151
- Hi.
- How are you feeling?

1424
00:52:19,546 --> 00:52:21,187
How are you feeling?

1425
00:52:21,633 --> 00:52:22,521
Tired.

1426
00:52:22,666 --> 00:52:24,698
- Tired?
- Yes.

1427
00:52:24,699 --> 00:52:26,792
They just went there, and they feel tired.

1428
00:52:26,793 --> 00:52:27,960
They're just tired.

1429
00:52:27,961 --> 00:52:30,298
- I've never heard that response before.
- I know, right?

1430
00:52:30,500 --> 00:52:33,165
- Usually, they say they're good.
- "I'm good."

1431
00:52:33,166 --> 00:52:34,800
Or they say, "Lovely."

1432
00:52:34,801 --> 00:52:35,935
- "Tired."
- "Tired."

1433
00:52:36,620 --> 00:52:38,204
That must be the boat.

1434
00:52:40,352 --> 00:52:43,776
(The boats are waiting to leave.)

1435
00:52:43,786 --> 00:52:45,478
It seems like we should take off
our shoes.

1436
00:52:45,752 --> 00:52:46,846
Into the water!

1437
00:52:46,939 --> 00:52:47,947
Into the water!

1438
00:52:48,086 --> 00:52:50,583
We have to keep our shoes off
until we get there.

1439
00:52:50,686 --> 00:52:52,686
Let's feel nature.

1440
00:52:52,687 --> 00:52:56,200
(Getting ready to get on the boat)

1441
00:52:56,492 --> 00:52:57,323
Oh, dear!

1442
00:52:58,132 --> 00:52:59,790
(Rolling away)

1443
00:53:01,663 --> 00:53:04,029
- I hope that doesn't happen in the ocean.
- Yes, girl!

1444
00:53:04,030 --> 00:53:05,865
- You did it!
- I caught it.

1445
00:53:05,866 --> 00:53:08,444
(The queens are so supportive.)

1446
00:53:09,001 --> 00:53:11,103
- Number nine!
- Is that it?

1447
00:53:11,770 --> 00:53:14,440
(They see Boat Number Nine.)

1448
00:53:15,174 --> 00:53:16,575
Hello.

1449
00:53:16,576 --> 00:53:19,145
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

1450
00:53:19,377 --> 00:53:20,570
Here you are.

1451
00:53:20,583 --> 00:53:21,981
We're riding boats a lot today.

1452
00:53:21,982 --> 00:53:23,415
- Thank you.
- Hello.

1453
00:53:23,617 --> 00:53:25,643
This boat isn't too rocky.

1454
00:53:25,644 --> 00:53:26,886
It feels safe.

1455
00:53:27,804 --> 00:53:29,804
It's nice. Look at nature over there.

1456
00:53:29,805 --> 00:53:31,357
It's so nice.

1457
00:53:31,504 --> 00:53:33,859
I've never been to a place
like this in Thailand before.

1458
00:53:33,860 --> 00:53:34,827
I know.

1459
00:53:34,828 --> 00:53:36,310
(The view looks refreshing from the boat.)

1460
00:53:36,311 --> 00:53:38,864
It's so nice! It's floating.

1461
00:53:39,560 --> 00:53:41,133
Dongdongju!

1462
00:53:43,480 --> 00:53:46,071
- Give me some dongdongju.
- Give me some dongdongju.

1463
00:53:46,072 --> 00:53:47,439
Floating!

1464
00:53:47,940 --> 00:53:49,147
(Roaring)

1465
00:53:49,173 --> 00:53:51,173
It'll be so much fun if it rains.

1466
00:53:51,174 --> 00:53:52,478
If it rains?

1467
00:53:52,899 --> 00:53:54,167
I'd enjoy it if it rained.

1468
00:53:54,213 --> 00:53:54,947
Me too.

1469
00:53:54,948 --> 00:53:56,948
I'd feel bad for the cameramen, though.

1470
00:53:57,220 --> 00:53:58,717
Let's go!

1471
00:53:58,980 --> 00:54:01,687
Okay. Number Nine takes off!

1472
00:54:02,380 --> 00:54:03,956
Here we go.

1473
00:54:04,140 --> 00:54:05,791
How nice!

1474
00:54:05,820 --> 00:54:07,426
Let's go!

1475
00:54:07,793 --> 00:54:09,395
It's cool.

1476
00:54:09,396 --> 00:54:12,153
(The cool sea breeze touches their faces.)

1477
00:54:12,154 --> 00:54:15,100
(Trilling)

1478
00:54:17,173 --> 00:54:20,067
(Imitating the motor boat)

1479
00:54:23,627 --> 00:54:25,077
So, this boat...

1480
00:54:25,280 --> 00:54:28,647
takes you past a peak
in just seven minutes.

1481
00:54:30,282 --> 00:54:32,218
- It takes 30 minutes on foot.
- If we didn't take this boat,

1482
00:54:32,219 --> 00:54:34,453
- we'd be walking up there.
- Yes.

1483
00:54:34,651 --> 00:54:37,251
(A 30-minute trekking route
in just 7 minutes)

1484
00:54:37,252 --> 00:54:38,724
What money can buy.

1485
00:54:40,969 --> 00:54:43,195
It's so refreshing!

1486
00:54:43,842 --> 00:54:44,830
It's cool!

1487
00:54:44,831 --> 00:54:47,369
(Nature's own natural mist)

1488
00:54:47,496 --> 00:54:49,235
Let's go!

1489
00:54:49,260 --> 00:54:51,127
I'm free!

1490
00:54:51,176 --> 00:54:54,206
I'm free! Oh, my gosh!

1491
00:54:55,689 --> 00:54:59,912
<i>I'm alive</i>

1492
00:55:05,457 --> 00:55:07,588
This song is "Alive" by Sia.

1493
00:55:07,649 --> 00:55:10,155
- I recommend it when you travel.
- Thanks.

1494
00:55:10,156 --> 00:55:11,290
- What do you think?
- I like it.

1495
00:55:11,291 --> 00:55:13,592
- "I'm so alive."
- It's good.

1496
00:55:13,636 --> 00:55:15,394
I'll check it out when I travel.

1497
00:55:15,395 --> 00:55:18,364
Let's go all the way there!

1498
00:55:18,365 --> 00:55:19,965
All the way to space!

1499
00:55:20,733 --> 00:55:23,002
We can't go that far!

1500
00:55:24,670 --> 00:55:28,140
- We're close. We're almost there.
- We're there.

1501
00:55:28,141 --> 00:55:29,875
It looks like a deserted island.

1502
00:55:30,576 --> 00:55:32,578
I feel like we're going
to a deserted island.

1503
00:55:32,831 --> 00:55:35,684
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1504
00:55:35,685 --> 00:55:37,783
(Singing)

1505
00:55:38,198 --> 00:55:40,084
(Getting off the boat)

1506
00:55:40,584 --> 00:55:43,138
(The meow queen also takes off.)

1507
00:55:43,318 --> 00:55:44,790
We've arrived on a deserted island.

1508
00:55:45,538 --> 00:55:47,538
It really feels like a deserted island.

1509
00:55:47,539 --> 00:55:50,344
- Thank you so much.
- Yes!

1510
00:55:50,584 --> 00:55:53,432
What's the one thing you'd bring
to a deserted island?

1511
00:55:53,732 --> 00:55:55,601
- That's insane.
- That's crazy. Only one?

1512
00:55:55,602 --> 00:55:57,870
- What should I bring?
- What do I bring?

1513
00:55:57,935 --> 00:56:00,205
This trip is...

1514
00:56:00,235 --> 00:56:01,340
kind of like that.

1515
00:56:01,609 --> 00:56:04,174
- I'd bring a water filter.
- A water filter?

1516
00:56:04,175 --> 00:56:05,611
That's so practical.

1517
00:56:05,642 --> 00:56:08,047
I'd bring a lighter.

1518
00:56:08,447 --> 00:56:11,150
- That sounds good.
- To make a fire.

1519
00:56:12,051 --> 00:56:13,719
I'd bring Won Ji.

1520
00:56:14,444 --> 00:56:15,888
She'd make us survive.

1521
00:56:16,488 --> 00:56:18,023
We could survive then.

1522
00:56:19,024 --> 00:56:20,326
Poor Won Ji.

1523
00:56:20,357 --> 00:56:22,761
- Poor me.
- That's not fair.

1524
00:56:22,791 --> 00:56:24,196
- That's not fair.
- Poor thing.

1525
00:56:24,511 --> 00:56:26,732
This is fun. I see a lot of branches.

1526
00:56:26,999 --> 00:56:28,167
Is it going to rain?

1527
00:56:29,097 --> 00:56:31,170
What if we get stranded here?

1528
00:56:31,926 --> 00:56:33,372
- Cute.
- There's a cat.

1529
00:56:33,706 --> 00:56:34,807
It looks like a kitten.

1530
00:56:36,052 --> 00:56:37,743
- It's coming.
- What?

1531
00:56:40,145 --> 00:56:42,281
- So cute.
- You are so friendly.

1532
00:56:42,439 --> 00:56:45,017
That's so cute.
What do you call a cat like that?

1533
00:56:45,284 --> 00:56:47,252
- A puppy-like cat.
- A puppy-like cat.

1534
00:56:48,721 --> 00:56:50,356
That cat is friendly like a dog.

1535
00:56:50,357 --> 00:56:53,057
- How cute.
- It's affectionate.

1536
00:56:53,058 --> 00:56:55,227
Come with us and guide us.

1537
00:56:55,431 --> 00:56:56,758
(Meowing)

1538
00:56:56,759 --> 00:56:58,097
- It's following us.
- It's following us.

1539
00:56:58,098 --> 00:56:59,398
Even the cat is...

1540
00:56:59,399 --> 00:57:01,266
- part of our cave exploration team!
- Guide us.

1541
00:57:01,298 --> 00:57:02,735
Cave Exploration Team!

1542
00:57:02,736 --> 00:57:04,336
- Cave.
- Exploration Team!

1543
00:57:04,491 --> 00:57:08,007
You can see both the ocean
and the forest here.

1544
00:57:08,544 --> 00:57:10,209
- You can enjoy them both.
- We can enjoy nature.

1545
00:57:10,431 --> 00:57:11,877
This place is nice.

1546
00:57:12,324 --> 00:57:13,331
It has a nice vibe.

1547
00:57:13,332 --> 00:57:15,881
- It's really pretty.
- I love it.

1548
00:57:16,178 --> 00:57:19,184
- I can smell the trees.
- I know. Fresh grass.

1549
00:57:19,424 --> 00:57:20,552
It smells like a forest.

1550
00:57:20,553 --> 00:57:22,758
(A grassy scent in the air)

1551
00:57:22,955 --> 00:57:24,523
I feel like this is the coolest place
in Thailand.

1552
00:57:24,544 --> 00:57:26,792
- It's indeed cool.
- It's not humid.

1553
00:57:27,311 --> 00:57:29,437
- Aren't you glad that we're here?
- I'm glad we came here.

1554
00:57:29,438 --> 00:57:31,824
- It's so nice.
- It's so therapeutic.

1555
00:57:31,825 --> 00:57:32,564
Right?

1556
00:57:32,565 --> 00:57:34,967
- We need to spend time in nature.
- It's beautiful.

1557
00:57:34,968 --> 00:57:35,901
Seriously.

1558
00:57:36,458 --> 00:57:39,705
There are many different types
of trees here.

1559
00:57:41,606 --> 00:57:44,109
I can handle 30 minutes
if it stays this flat.

1560
00:57:44,376 --> 00:57:45,944
Does anyone like hiking?

1561
00:57:46,199 --> 00:57:47,159
(Quiet)

1562
00:57:47,160 --> 00:57:48,087
I guess not.

1563
00:57:48,480 --> 00:57:50,482
I'm kind of into hiking.

1564
00:57:51,183 --> 00:57:53,552
I like the sound of birds.

1565
00:57:53,774 --> 00:57:55,754
Your face kind of reminds me of a bird.

1566
00:57:56,321 --> 00:57:59,591
I look a little bit like everything.

1567
00:57:59,592 --> 00:58:01,172
I look like a bird.

1568
00:58:01,173 --> 00:58:02,239
What else?

1569
00:58:02,260 --> 00:58:04,696
I also look like a jellyfish.

1570
00:58:04,897 --> 00:58:07,833
- A jellyfish?
- That's cute. It suits you.

1571
00:58:07,834 --> 00:58:08,867
There's a lizard.

1572
00:58:09,039 --> 00:58:10,102
- Where?
- Where?

1573
00:58:10,103 --> 00:58:12,349
I love lizards!

1574
00:58:12,430 --> 00:58:14,039
Come home with me!

1575
00:58:14,406 --> 00:58:15,674
I have to take a picture.

1576
00:58:15,870 --> 00:58:17,870
This is like a jungle.

1577
00:58:18,844 --> 00:58:20,879
I love them!

1578
00:58:20,957 --> 00:58:22,514
(Harimu fell in love.)

1579
00:58:22,515 --> 00:58:24,583
- Can you take a picture of me?
- It went in!

1580
00:58:24,817 --> 00:58:26,385
I'm not a good photographer.

1581
00:58:26,386 --> 00:58:27,491
(Disappearing)

1582
00:58:28,620 --> 00:58:30,322
It went into the hole.

1583
00:58:31,090 --> 00:58:33,090
- A video.
- That must be its home.

1584
00:58:33,125 --> 00:58:34,426
I couldn't take a video.

1585
00:58:34,427 --> 00:58:35,494
Gabee.

1586
00:58:36,004 --> 00:58:39,398
(A picture with the lizard's home)

1587
00:58:39,400 --> 00:58:41,086
I love lizards so much.

1588
00:58:41,087 --> 00:58:42,434
That's its house.

1589
00:58:42,435 --> 00:58:43,168
Good night.

1590
00:58:43,169 --> 00:58:44,887
You got a picture with its tail.

1591
00:58:44,888 --> 00:58:46,407
- Nice.
- You can see the tail.

1592
00:58:46,408 --> 00:58:47,940
- I love their tails.
- That's its house.

1593
00:58:48,294 --> 00:58:50,209
Hold on.

1594
00:58:50,210 --> 00:58:52,219
I see something in front of us.

1595
00:58:52,220 --> 00:58:54,546
I found a massive rock!

1596
00:58:54,853 --> 00:58:57,061
There are some stone steps.

1597
00:58:57,062 --> 00:58:58,984
We have to climb them.

1598
00:59:00,066 --> 00:59:02,554
It almost looks like a cliff.

1599
00:59:02,711 --> 00:59:05,757
It says it's only 430m up.

1600
00:59:06,691 --> 00:59:09,161
The other one was 2km,
but this one is 430m.

1601
00:59:09,162 --> 00:59:10,596
That's amazing.

1602
00:59:10,597 --> 00:59:12,297
You know I hiked in the Himalayas.

1603
00:59:12,298 --> 00:59:13,866
You've been to the Himalayas?

1604
00:59:13,867 --> 00:59:15,400
I have. It's so easy.

1605
00:59:15,675 --> 00:59:17,612
- It's so easy.
- That's impressive.

1606
00:59:17,613 --> 00:59:19,685
(Won Ji hiked in the Himalayas.)

1607
00:59:19,874 --> 00:59:23,626
Since I hiked in the Himalayas,
this won't be a problem.

1608
00:59:23,651 --> 00:59:25,410
A woman who hiked in the Himalayas!

1609
00:59:25,411 --> 00:59:26,979
- The Himalayas!
- She's been there!

1610
00:59:26,980 --> 00:59:28,579
- Gangnam woman.
- Gangnam woman.

1611
00:59:28,600 --> 00:59:32,017
A human as rough as the Himalayas!
Himalaya Woman!

1612
00:59:34,080 --> 00:59:38,590
They make a song out of everything.

1613
00:59:38,690 --> 00:59:39,925
I don't understand them either.

1614
00:59:40,420 --> 00:59:41,260
I don't know.

1615
00:59:41,261 --> 00:59:43,695
I've been trying hard since yesterday.

1616
00:59:43,696 --> 00:59:44,897
I'm so excited.

1617
00:59:46,601 --> 00:59:50,260
- Himalaya Woman!
- Himalaya Woman!

1618
00:59:50,736 --> 00:59:53,272
Won Ji, now you're Himalaya Woman.
I love it.

1619
00:59:53,407 --> 00:59:56,909
A woman with glasses
who hiked in the Himalayas.

1620
00:59:57,532 --> 00:59:58,875
(Out of breath)

1621
00:59:58,942 --> 01:00:03,399
I'm a Himalayan girl!

1622
01:00:03,400 --> 01:00:05,267
I could never get used to that energy.

1623
01:00:05,268 --> 01:00:06,802
That's top-tier energy.

1624
01:00:08,772 --> 01:00:10,540
(Korean top-tier energy)

1625
01:00:10,540 --> 01:00:12,307
Let's go!

1626
01:00:12,442 --> 01:00:13,475
Do the tongue thing.

1627
01:00:13,476 --> 01:00:15,611
(Growling)

1628
01:00:15,612 --> 01:00:16,445
(Cute ending)

1629
01:00:17,147 --> 01:00:17,980
Let's go.

1630
01:00:17,981 --> 01:00:20,549
Okay, calm down for a second.

1631
01:00:20,684 --> 01:00:23,052
- Let's go.
- Okay.

1632
01:00:23,053 --> 01:00:24,053
(Heading out before sunset)

1633
01:00:24,321 --> 01:00:26,188
How about a team cheer?

1634
01:00:26,189 --> 01:00:27,690
Let's shout "Himalayas" when we climb.

1635
01:00:27,691 --> 01:00:28,791
I like that.

1636
01:00:29,526 --> 01:00:31,227
- Like this, "Himalayas!"
- Love it.

1637
01:00:31,228 --> 01:00:32,394
(This is nothing compared
to the Himalayas.)

1638
01:00:32,395 --> 01:00:33,295
Ready.

1639
01:00:33,597 --> 01:00:35,397
- Himalayas!
- Himalayas!

1640
01:00:35,533 --> 01:00:36,432
Let's go!

1641
01:00:36,433 --> 01:00:38,701
- Okay.
- When we swim in the ocean?

1642
01:00:39,036 --> 01:00:40,123
Little Mermaid!

1643
01:00:40,124 --> 01:00:41,437
(An awkward moment for the Himalaya girl.)

1644
01:00:41,605 --> 01:00:43,372
It's more fun like this.

1645
01:00:43,373 --> 01:00:44,607
Feels like we're getting healthier.

1646
01:00:44,608 --> 01:00:45,942
(Finally setting off for the cave)

1647
01:00:45,943 --> 01:00:47,944
- Please watch your step.
- We could slip and fall.

1648
01:00:47,945 --> 01:00:50,446
We need to take this seriously.

1649
01:00:50,480 --> 01:00:51,447
Serious mode, girls.

1650
01:00:51,448 --> 01:00:53,282
(A sudden change in attitude)

1651
01:00:53,650 --> 01:00:55,951
(The oldest finds it all hilarious.)

1652
01:00:56,520 --> 01:00:57,854
It's definitely steep.

1653
01:00:58,155 --> 01:00:59,355
We've barely even started climbing.

1654
01:01:00,323 --> 01:01:01,189
It's steep.

1655
01:01:01,691 --> 01:01:03,358
So steep.

1656
01:01:03,359 --> 01:01:05,327
(A short but steep climb)

1657
01:01:05,696 --> 01:01:07,429
We're getting closer to the sky.

1658
01:01:08,765 --> 01:01:10,099
Be careful.

1659
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:11,567
We need to be more serious.

1660
01:01:11,868 --> 01:01:14,536
We need to be serious.
We have to be careful.

1661
01:01:16,274 --> 01:01:19,142
- Right?
- We can't laugh. It's dangerous.

1662
01:01:19,143 --> 01:01:20,576
Why not?

1663
01:01:21,378 --> 01:01:22,978
It's like a try-not-to-laugh challenge.

1664
01:01:22,979 --> 01:01:25,848
(No one's laughing on a slope this steep.)

1665
01:01:26,583 --> 01:01:27,616
I'm already tired.

1666
01:01:28,785 --> 01:01:30,620
(Destination)

1667
01:01:30,621 --> 01:01:31,987
Slow and steady.

1668
01:01:33,457 --> 01:01:36,526
(Current location)

1669
01:01:37,027 --> 01:01:40,396
(There's still a long way to go.)

1670
01:01:40,997 --> 01:01:42,030
I'm so happy right now.

1671
01:01:42,031 --> 01:01:43,499
How's the pace, everyone?

1672
01:01:43,500 --> 01:01:44,733
- Good.
- Good.

1673
01:01:44,734 --> 01:01:45,634
All right.

1674
01:01:46,403 --> 01:01:48,170
When are we ever going to be
in a place like this?

1675
01:01:48,171 --> 01:01:49,305
(If you can't avoid it, enjoy it!)

1676
01:01:49,306 --> 01:01:51,040
I'll enjoy it while I can.

1677
01:01:51,475 --> 01:01:52,275
Enjoy it.

1678
01:01:53,843 --> 01:01:56,118
(She pauses to let the others catch up.)

1679
01:01:56,646 --> 01:01:58,780
What is that?

1680
01:01:59,449 --> 01:02:00,582
What is it?

1681
01:02:01,852 --> 01:02:03,352
Oh, dear!

1682
01:02:03,353 --> 01:02:04,587
(Endless stone steps)

1683
01:02:04,588 --> 01:02:05,441
Still got a long way to go.

1684
01:02:05,989 --> 01:02:07,156
I'm falling behind!

1685
01:02:08,025 --> 01:02:09,091
Someone's falling behind.

1686
01:02:09,092 --> 01:02:09,992
No, you can't.

1687
01:02:10,594 --> 01:02:11,320
Any second now.

1688
01:02:11,321 --> 01:02:12,295
(Himalaya girl is falling behind?)

1689
01:02:12,296 --> 01:02:13,930
There's still a long way to go,

1690
01:02:14,297 --> 01:02:15,464
but I think I'll be fine.

1691
01:02:15,899 --> 01:02:17,466
Positive energy!

1692
01:02:17,467 --> 01:02:19,435
Absolutely positive!

1693
01:02:19,436 --> 01:02:20,903
Positive!

1694
01:02:20,904 --> 01:02:22,838
Energy!

1695
01:02:23,406 --> 01:02:25,907
(They must be tired too.)

1696
01:02:26,442 --> 01:02:29,211
I think I've already gotten
a bunch of bug bites.

1697
01:02:30,847 --> 01:02:32,481
My knees are itchy.

1698
01:02:33,150 --> 01:02:34,884
I feel like my ears are gonna pop.

1699
01:02:34,885 --> 01:02:35,819
(Can't handle the itching)

1700
01:02:35,820 --> 01:02:37,420
My knees are itchy.

1701
01:02:37,487 --> 01:02:38,587
Slowly.

1702
01:02:39,256 --> 01:02:40,991
You just need to take one step at a time.

1703
01:02:40,992 --> 01:02:42,124
They're dancers, all right.

1704
01:02:42,325 --> 01:02:43,191
You will eventually get there.

1705
01:02:43,894 --> 01:02:45,461
(How a queen hikes.)

1706
01:02:45,462 --> 01:02:46,829
She's hiking with her nails up?

1707
01:02:47,531 --> 01:02:49,464
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

1708
01:02:50,533 --> 01:02:51,700
It doesn't seem like it.

1709
01:02:51,701 --> 01:02:52,701
No, I'm fine.

1710
01:02:53,370 --> 01:02:54,570
It's so hot.

1711
01:02:55,305 --> 01:02:57,306
I think we're halfway there.

1712
01:02:57,307 --> 01:02:59,108
Already half?

1713
01:02:59,109 --> 01:03:00,909
- This isn't too bad!
- Maybe?

1714
01:03:01,611 --> 01:03:03,145
I've climbed the Himalayas!

1715
01:03:03,347 --> 01:03:05,781
Himalaya girl!

1716
01:03:06,283 --> 01:03:08,017
(Oops)

1717
01:03:08,351 --> 01:03:10,151
Not a Gangnam girl!

1718
01:03:10,152 --> 01:03:13,188
I'm a Himalaya girl!

1719
01:03:14,324 --> 01:03:16,492
I'm a Himalaya girl.

1720
01:03:17,260 --> 01:03:18,727
You've got this, Won Ji.

1721
01:03:21,198 --> 01:03:22,632
I hate mountains.

1722
01:03:22,633 --> 01:03:23,566
- Why?
- I hate hiking.

1723
01:03:23,967 --> 01:03:26,135
That's right. You said you don't
really like working out.

1724
01:03:26,604 --> 01:03:27,703
To my future boyfriend,

1725
01:03:27,704 --> 01:03:29,038
if you ask me to go hiking with you...

1726
01:03:30,173 --> 01:03:31,773
It's goodbye.

1727
01:03:31,774 --> 01:03:32,608
Really?

1728
01:03:33,042 --> 01:03:34,843
There's a rest area here.
Let's take a break.

1729
01:03:36,313 --> 01:03:37,647
There's a rest area?

1730
01:03:38,248 --> 01:03:40,049
- You can see the ocean!
- Let's take a quick look.

1731
01:03:40,417 --> 01:03:41,784
Gosh!

1732
01:03:41,918 --> 01:03:42,784
So beautiful.

1733
01:03:42,785 --> 01:03:43,619
(A scenic rest stop)

1734
01:03:44,821 --> 01:03:46,221
Look at this view!

1735
01:03:46,790 --> 01:03:48,023
Wow, it's so pretty.

1736
01:03:48,425 --> 01:03:50,426
We walked all the way from there to here?

1737
01:03:51,127 --> 01:03:52,027
That's crazy.

1738
01:03:52,629 --> 01:03:54,697
Woo-hoo!

1739
01:03:54,698 --> 01:03:56,265
Yabba-dabba-doo!

1740
01:03:57,367 --> 01:03:58,133
Wow.

1741
01:04:01,071 --> 01:04:02,004
This is the summit, right?

1742
01:04:02,939 --> 01:04:04,006
I think we're almost there.

1743
01:04:04,007 --> 01:04:05,073
Maybe 230 meters?

1744
01:04:05,074 --> 01:04:06,275
We're halfway there.

1745
01:04:07,110 --> 01:04:08,510
Isn't this the cave?

1746
01:04:09,246 --> 01:04:10,913
I think this is the cave.

1747
01:04:11,081 --> 01:04:12,982
I'm sweating so much.

1748
01:04:12,983 --> 01:04:13,883
I'm sweating like crazy!

1749
01:04:15,018 --> 01:04:17,319
But this feels so good.

1750
01:04:17,821 --> 01:04:18,654
Look at the mountains.

1751
01:04:18,655 --> 01:04:20,156
(The sea breeze cools the sweat away.)

1752
01:04:20,157 --> 01:04:21,290
Wow, that looks amazing.

1753
01:04:21,758 --> 01:04:23,093
Gosh.

1754
01:04:23,094 --> 01:04:24,326
You think that's really a deserted island?

1755
01:04:25,328 --> 01:04:26,295
(If you're done cooling down,)

1756
01:04:26,296 --> 01:04:27,229
Let's go now.

1757
01:04:27,597 --> 01:04:28,497
All right!

1758
01:04:28,498 --> 01:04:29,531
Back to it!

1759
01:04:29,532 --> 01:04:31,867
(let's go!)

1760
01:04:32,235 --> 01:04:33,735
I'm sweating like crazy.

1761
01:04:33,736 --> 01:04:34,570
(Back to sweating buckets)

1762
01:04:34,571 --> 01:04:36,605
I don't even sweat this much
when I'm dancing.

1763
01:04:36,606 --> 01:04:37,539
- Really?
- Yes.

1764
01:04:37,607 --> 01:04:38,740
I barely ever sweat.

1765
01:04:39,576 --> 01:04:40,464
Right now, it's dripping.

1766
01:04:40,465 --> 01:04:41,645
(A tough trail that makes anyone sweat)

1767
01:04:41,879 --> 01:04:43,546
Those foreigners were so funny.

1768
01:04:43,547 --> 01:04:44,713
(The tourists before the boat ride)

1769
01:04:44,714 --> 01:04:45,714
"Are you feeling good?"

1770
01:04:46,616 --> 01:04:47,382
"Tired."

1771
01:04:49,519 --> 01:04:50,452
I get it now.

1772
01:04:50,754 --> 01:04:53,322
- We get it now!
- Now, I get it!

1773
01:04:53,323 --> 01:04:54,190
I'm losing it.

1774
01:04:55,359 --> 01:04:56,692
This is not what I expected.

1775
01:04:57,394 --> 01:04:58,794
It wasn't like this when I looked it up.

1776
01:04:59,896 --> 01:05:00,896
We are...

1777
01:05:01,464 --> 01:05:03,331
falling behind.

1778
01:05:04,167 --> 01:05:05,567
Is anyone there?

1779
01:05:05,568 --> 01:05:06,435
Nope.

1780
01:05:06,770 --> 01:05:08,504
Oh, no. We actually fell behind.

1781
01:05:08,872 --> 01:05:09,872
- It's okay.
- We can do this!

1782
01:05:10,073 --> 01:05:11,273
Wow, it's echoing.

1783
01:05:11,274 --> 01:05:12,508
We can do this!

1784
01:05:12,675 --> 01:05:15,778
Of course you can.
There's nothing you can't do.

1785
01:05:15,779 --> 01:05:16,845
(The queen keeps dropping gems.)

1786
01:05:17,147 --> 01:05:20,182
Seriously, this is a record amount
of sweat for me.

1787
01:05:20,850 --> 01:05:22,517
- Wow, I can see that!
- I'm serious.

1788
01:05:22,518 --> 01:05:24,419
I bet you don't even sweat
like that in a sauna.

1789
01:05:24,420 --> 01:05:26,515
No, I really don't.

1790
01:05:26,516 --> 01:05:27,656
(Looking like she just washed her face)

1791
01:05:28,491 --> 01:05:31,326
Okay, it's downhill from here.

1792
01:05:31,327 --> 01:05:33,662
- Hang in there!
- It's downhill now.

1793
01:05:34,898 --> 01:05:36,932
- Cheer up.
- Yes, downhill!

1794
01:05:36,933 --> 01:05:38,467
You've got this.

1795
01:05:39,636 --> 01:05:40,703
Why are they so good at this?

1796
01:05:40,704 --> 01:05:42,571
(Their energy is unreal.)

1797
01:05:43,238 --> 01:05:44,706
(Another tourist spotted ahead.)

1798
01:05:45,107 --> 01:05:46,908
The cave?

1799
01:05:47,377 --> 01:05:49,078
- It's really nice.
- Really?

1800
01:05:49,079 --> 01:05:50,079
Nice.

1801
01:05:50,080 --> 01:05:51,046
Is it worth it?

1802
01:05:51,247 --> 01:05:52,414
Worth the journey.

1803
01:05:52,415 --> 01:05:53,582
Okay, perfect.

1804
01:05:53,651 --> 01:05:54,950
<i>Baby, you're worth it.</i>

1805
01:05:55,118 --> 01:05:56,318
(Singing along)

1806
01:05:56,686 --> 01:05:57,619
Worth it!

1807
01:05:57,620 --> 01:05:59,921
(Starting up again!)

1808
01:06:02,459 --> 01:06:04,113
They're staring at us.

1809
01:06:04,114 --> 01:06:05,428
(The tourists from earlier turned around.)

1810
01:06:05,628 --> 01:06:06,695
My friends...

1811
01:06:07,330 --> 01:06:08,163
are crazy.

1812
01:06:09,666 --> 01:06:11,000
My friends are crazy.

1813
01:06:12,836 --> 01:06:15,304
(Singing)

1814
01:06:15,305 --> 01:06:15,971
(Birds chirping)

1815
01:06:15,972 --> 01:06:16,806
That's right.

1816
01:06:19,142 --> 01:06:19,942
Okay.

1817
01:06:20,477 --> 01:06:21,310
Okay.

1818
01:06:21,778 --> 01:06:23,412
Hold on.

1819
01:06:24,147 --> 01:06:26,882
(Even birds chirping gets her dancing.)

1820
01:06:27,417 --> 01:06:28,952
(The birds are silent.)

1821
01:06:28,953 --> 01:06:30,019
Give me the beat.

1822
01:06:30,788 --> 01:06:31,754
Give me the beat!

1823
01:06:31,755 --> 01:06:33,756
Oh, my gosh. Bird, work it.

1824
01:06:33,757 --> 01:06:35,691
- Work it.
- She wants to dance.

1825
01:06:35,692 --> 01:06:37,426
(There's no music.)

1826
01:06:37,961 --> 01:06:41,297
(It doesn't matter.)

1827
01:06:41,798 --> 01:06:43,699
I want to live like Harimu.

1828
01:06:43,700 --> 01:06:44,700
(Harimu is my new role model.)

1829
01:06:44,701 --> 01:06:45,634
Life would be so fun.

1830
01:06:47,170 --> 01:06:50,906
(It really is so much fun, Won Ji.)

1831
01:06:50,907 --> 01:06:51,874
You're so good.

1832
01:06:52,575 --> 01:06:54,543
I'm so proud of you, Harimu.

1833
01:06:55,311 --> 01:06:56,945
We're almost there. I can see the sign.

1834
01:06:56,946 --> 01:07:00,415
Oh, I think we're all done.

1835
01:07:00,550 --> 01:07:02,117
- Done?
- Yes.

1836
01:07:02,118 --> 01:07:02,884
Done?

1837
01:07:03,586 --> 01:07:06,555
- You can already feel the cool air.
- We did it.

1838
01:07:06,556 --> 01:07:07,789
That wasn't so bad.

1839
01:07:07,924 --> 01:07:08,657
We did it.

1840
01:07:09,059 --> 01:07:10,992
This is how all horror movies start.

1841
01:07:10,993 --> 01:07:12,928
No!

1842
01:07:13,997 --> 01:07:15,030
Where are we?

1843
01:07:15,899 --> 01:07:16,799
What's that?

1844
01:07:17,667 --> 01:07:18,867
Let's go find out.

1845
01:07:18,868 --> 01:07:20,470
(Curiosity usually ends in disaster.)

1846
01:07:20,471 --> 01:07:21,770
This is how it starts, right?

1847
01:07:23,440 --> 01:07:24,273
Amazing.

1848
01:07:24,774 --> 01:07:26,274
Goodness.

1849
01:07:26,275 --> 01:07:27,176
I'm scared!

1850
01:07:27,677 --> 01:07:29,411
- This place feels eerie.
- True.

1851
01:07:29,412 --> 01:07:32,381
(Things are suddenly getting spooky.)

1852
01:07:32,382 --> 01:07:34,783
You know Thai ghosts are
the scariest, right?

1853
01:07:35,318 --> 01:07:38,054
Yes, there are tons of haunted spots
in Thailand.

1854
01:07:38,055 --> 01:07:39,354
- Really?
- Haunted points?

1855
01:07:39,355 --> 01:07:41,890
I heard there's some dark energy here.

1856
01:07:42,292 --> 01:07:43,125
For real?

1857
01:07:43,559 --> 01:07:46,161
I'll fight it off with my bright energy!

1858
01:07:47,163 --> 01:07:49,030
- I bet they'll all run away.
- But that's...

1859
01:07:49,031 --> 01:07:50,299
what they say
at the beginning of the movie.

1860
01:07:50,300 --> 01:07:51,133
Right?

1861
01:07:51,401 --> 01:07:52,735
"I will fight them off!"

1862
01:07:52,736 --> 01:07:54,356
(The one in front gets caught first.)

1863
01:07:56,172 --> 01:07:57,205
What's that sound?

1864
01:07:59,108 --> 01:08:00,408
- What?
- That's crazy.

1865
01:08:00,409 --> 01:08:01,509
Gosh!

1866
01:08:01,510 --> 01:08:02,744
That is unreal.

1867
01:08:05,148 --> 01:08:06,582
The top part is beautiful.

1868
01:08:06,583 --> 01:08:08,984
(A breathtaking view)

1869
01:08:08,985 --> 01:08:10,552
It really is a cave.

1870
01:08:14,491 --> 01:08:17,793
(Mesmerized by the view)

1871
01:08:18,795 --> 01:08:25,901
(Stunning views right from the entrance)

1872
01:08:26,870 --> 01:08:28,071
Let's go. This is so cool.

1873
01:08:28,371 --> 01:08:30,238
It's so cool. I think it'll be
really cool in there.

1874
01:08:30,506 --> 01:08:32,340
Are you for real, Earth?

1875
01:08:33,309 --> 01:08:34,342
What in the world, Earth?

1876
01:08:34,978 --> 01:08:36,779
"What in the world, Earth?"

1877
01:08:36,913 --> 01:08:37,780
"W.W.E."

1878
01:08:37,781 --> 01:08:39,548
Well done, Earth.

1879
01:08:39,549 --> 01:08:41,517
(Moving along
with some brand new exclamations.)

1880
01:08:42,619 --> 01:08:45,054
It's a jungle down there.

1881
01:08:46,489 --> 01:08:48,290
There's a jungle.

1882
01:08:48,291 --> 01:08:51,359
(Lush greenery stretching out
like a jungle.)

1883
01:08:51,360 --> 01:08:52,227
It's a jungle.

1884
01:08:52,228 --> 01:08:56,665
(Immediately singing a jungle song)

1885
01:08:56,935 --> 01:08:58,133
Jungle girls.

1886
01:08:58,134 --> 01:08:59,601
Wow, this is nature at its finest.

1887
01:08:59,602 --> 01:09:02,938
(A wonder created by nature)

1888
01:09:05,174 --> 01:09:06,641
There's a dog here too.

1889
01:09:07,143 --> 01:09:08,677
How did you even get here?

1890
01:09:08,678 --> 01:09:10,479
I think he's guiding us.

1891
01:09:10,480 --> 01:09:11,880
(A little guide leading the way.)

1892
01:09:12,015 --> 01:09:14,049
These were able to grow...

1893
01:09:14,751 --> 01:09:16,051
because the sunlight can get in.

1894
01:09:16,052 --> 01:09:18,120
- You're right.
- Even though it's a cave.

1895
01:09:18,121 --> 01:09:19,755
Because there's water and sunlight.

1896
01:09:19,756 --> 01:09:20,756
Yes.

1897
01:09:22,192 --> 01:09:24,459
It's so worth the journey.

1898
01:09:25,461 --> 01:09:26,795
Where's the pavilion?

1899
01:09:26,796 --> 01:09:28,630
Maybe it's a little farther ahead.

1900
01:09:29,099 --> 01:09:31,032
It's so cool in here.

1901
01:09:31,033 --> 01:09:32,100
It definitely is cooler.

1902
01:09:32,101 --> 01:09:35,036
(Making their way to the pavilion
from the photos.)

1903
01:09:36,105 --> 01:09:37,338
It's over there!

1904
01:09:37,441 --> 01:09:39,975
- I think I see it!
- I see the pavilion.

1905
01:09:39,976 --> 01:09:41,076
(Something comes into view.)

1906
01:09:41,077 --> 01:09:42,744
Wow, this place is amazing.

1907
01:09:43,179 --> 01:09:45,314
- This feels really surreal.
- Like a horror experience.

1908
01:09:46,649 --> 01:09:47,716
It really feels like a cave now.

1909
01:09:47,785 --> 01:09:49,150
I can do it.

1910
01:09:50,920 --> 01:09:53,855
It's so big.

1911
01:09:55,858 --> 01:09:57,659
Gosh!

1912
01:09:58,556 --> 01:10:01,463
- This is crazy.
- Unbelievable.

1913
01:10:06,683 --> 01:10:09,016
(A pavilion inside a massive cave)

1914
01:10:09,017 --> 01:10:10,746
This place feels unbelievably vast.

1915
01:10:15,428 --> 01:10:19,234
(Sunlight pours
through a gigantic sinkhole.)

1916
01:10:20,672 --> 01:10:25,792
(Beneath it stands a pavilion.)

1917
01:10:26,712 --> 01:10:30,059
(A mysterious historical site hidden
inside the cave)

1918
01:10:31,492 --> 01:10:40,255
(Traditional architecture can be
seen throughout.)

1919
01:10:40,489 --> 01:10:43,045
This is so nice.

1920
01:10:43,222 --> 01:10:46,515
- We made it.
- We made it.

1921
01:10:46,722 --> 01:10:48,383
If you put your mind to it, you can do it.

1922
01:10:50,018 --> 01:10:52,321
- It was worth it.
- Right.

1923
01:10:52,760 --> 01:10:54,272
We're amazing.

1924
01:10:54,273 --> 01:10:56,992
- I made it.
- Great job, everyone.

1925
01:10:58,760 --> 01:11:00,996
This is so overwhelming.

1926
01:11:01,263 --> 01:11:02,798
Everything blends together perfectly.

1927
01:11:02,984 --> 01:11:05,134
The scenery behind it is just...

1928
01:11:06,668 --> 01:11:08,570
It feels like if you make
a wish here, it'll come true.

1929
01:11:09,605 --> 01:11:11,406
It has such a commanding presence.

1930
01:11:11,407 --> 01:11:13,881
(Everyone feels naturally solemn.)

1931
01:11:13,882 --> 01:11:16,211
It's even better because it's so quiet.

1932
01:11:22,094 --> 01:11:23,452
It's really quiet here.

1933
01:11:23,453 --> 01:11:25,721
I feel like we shouldn't talk loudly.

1934
01:11:25,722 --> 01:11:27,823
(Whispering)

1935
01:11:27,824 --> 01:11:29,091
It's really cool.

1936
01:11:30,359 --> 01:11:32,961
- This dog is so cute.
- Should we take a picture with the dog?

1937
01:11:33,239 --> 01:11:34,299
How are we supposed to take one?

1938
01:11:34,300 --> 01:11:35,397
- Like this.
- I got it.

1939
01:11:36,785 --> 01:11:37,833
Look over here.

1940
01:11:38,579 --> 01:11:40,525
(Snapping a shot)

1941
01:11:40,665 --> 01:11:41,799
All done.

1942
01:11:41,800 --> 01:11:43,305
- It's so cute.
- It's great.

1943
01:11:43,306 --> 01:11:44,673
It's really great.

1944
01:11:44,712 --> 01:11:45,741
Want to come home with me?

1945
01:11:46,408 --> 01:11:47,943
Should we film a Reel here?

1946
01:11:48,335 --> 01:11:50,788
Should we do our stepping challenge here?

1947
01:11:50,789 --> 01:11:51,947
Yes, let's do it.

1948
01:11:53,182 --> 01:11:56,181
(It starts with the stepping scene.)

1949
01:11:59,801 --> 01:12:02,729
(Stepping again)

1950
01:12:02,730 --> 01:12:04,664
(The stepping Reel so far)

1951
01:12:04,744 --> 01:12:06,295
Hello.

1952
01:12:17,751 --> 01:12:19,975
- You're so good.
- We click so well.

1953
01:12:19,976 --> 01:12:22,071
- Should we check out the back?
- Good idea.

1954
01:12:22,072 --> 01:12:23,946
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

1955
01:12:24,842 --> 01:12:27,449
It feels like we're exploring the jungle.

1956
01:12:27,983 --> 01:12:29,722
It's like a jungle expedition.

1957
01:12:29,723 --> 01:12:34,009
(They take a full lap
around the pavilion.)

1958
01:12:37,025 --> 01:12:38,694
It's so round.

1959
01:12:38,967 --> 01:12:40,967
- Look at that.
- It's so nice.

1960
01:12:41,787 --> 01:12:45,320
It's amazing that there's a forest
inside a cave.

1961
01:12:45,321 --> 01:12:48,170
Two things that don't seem
to belong together.

1962
01:12:48,308 --> 01:12:49,638
- It's beautiful.
- So cool.

1963
01:12:49,639 --> 01:12:51,861
(Mesmerized)

1964
01:12:53,208 --> 01:12:55,310
This is actually the front.

1965
01:12:55,614 --> 01:12:58,614
The sunlight hits this side.

1966
01:12:58,615 --> 01:13:00,182
So this is the front.

1967
01:13:00,183 --> 01:13:01,583
- It is the front.
- I see.

1968
01:13:01,584 --> 01:13:02,684
It's huge.

1969
01:13:02,685 --> 01:13:05,187
How did they ever bring this here?

1970
01:13:05,248 --> 01:13:07,322
Exactly, that's incredible.

1971
01:13:07,589 --> 01:13:09,353
People will probably think
it's a mystery someday.

1972
01:13:09,354 --> 01:13:11,440
(Even getting up here is difficult.)

1973
01:13:11,441 --> 01:13:12,794
Maybe in a hundred million years?

1974
01:13:12,940 --> 01:13:14,997
I think that's where people make wishes.

1975
01:13:16,298 --> 01:13:18,298
I hope theirs comes true.

1976
01:13:19,034 --> 01:13:21,034
May it come true.

1977
01:13:21,203 --> 01:13:22,804
Let's make one too.

1978
01:13:22,938 --> 01:13:24,306
Let's go over there.

1979
01:13:24,518 --> 01:13:26,007
- Okay.
- Good idea.

1980
01:13:26,008 --> 01:13:27,376
I think there's a path.

1981
01:13:28,977 --> 01:13:30,512
This place is so spacious.

1982
01:13:31,563 --> 01:13:33,098
This is incredible.

1983
01:13:33,099 --> 01:13:35,086
(More breathtaking scenery appears
around every corner.)

1984
01:13:35,111 --> 01:13:36,385
It's so spacious.

1985
01:13:36,919 --> 01:13:37,953
This place is incredible.

1986
01:13:37,954 --> 01:13:40,355
It feels like someone built
a giant aquarium.

1987
01:13:40,739 --> 01:13:42,024
- Absolutely.
- Right?

1988
01:13:42,025 --> 01:13:45,412
(Feeling like a tiny fish in a fishbowl)

1989
01:13:46,947 --> 01:13:49,130
- It's cool in here.
- It feels so good.

1990
01:13:49,197 --> 01:13:50,198
This was so worth it.

1991
01:13:50,247 --> 01:13:52,067
We worked up a sweat
climbing all the way here.

1992
01:13:52,240 --> 01:13:53,860
I've never seen anything like this before.

1993
01:13:53,861 --> 01:13:56,738
We crossed the sea
and climbed the mountain.

1994
01:13:57,027 --> 01:13:59,824
Normally, after something like this,
you have a beer.

1995
01:13:59,825 --> 01:14:01,543
That would be perfect.

1996
01:14:01,544 --> 01:14:02,878
After working this hard, it's even better.

1997
01:14:03,442 --> 01:14:04,684
A gift from nature.

1998
01:14:04,709 --> 01:14:05,905
(A lesson in patience,
learned in Thailand)

1999
01:14:05,930 --> 01:14:08,516
- I saw people praying here earlier.
- I know.

2000
01:14:08,517 --> 01:14:11,052
Let's pray too.
You know those stone cairns, right?

2001
01:14:11,053 --> 01:14:12,120
Should we do it there?

2002
01:14:12,121 --> 01:14:15,245
Let's wish for Abra-ca-Empty
to become a huge success.

2003
01:14:15,246 --> 01:14:16,458
Good idea.

2004
01:14:16,526 --> 01:14:18,762
- The number one ratings in our time slot.
- Great idea.

2005
01:14:19,013 --> 01:14:20,633
That's actually a great idea.

2006
01:14:20,634 --> 01:14:22,631
Everyone, go find one stone you like.

2007
01:14:22,632 --> 01:14:25,132
(A huge one)

2008
01:14:25,133 --> 01:14:26,234
Isn't that a boulder?

2009
01:14:26,439 --> 01:14:28,103
Here's mine.

2010
01:14:28,104 --> 01:14:30,306
(Won Ji also places a stone.)

2011
01:14:30,586 --> 01:14:33,032
Mine's pretty big,
so I'll stack mine first.

2012
01:14:35,287 --> 01:14:36,211
Very good.

2013
01:14:36,212 --> 01:14:38,550
It needs to be built the hard way.

2014
01:14:38,551 --> 01:14:40,344
- I'll stack it here again.
- Wait.

2015
01:14:40,345 --> 01:14:42,951
(They're getting serious
about building the cairn.)

2016
01:14:43,477 --> 01:14:44,653
Is this okay?

2017
01:14:44,730 --> 01:14:45,520
(Gently)

2018
01:14:45,887 --> 01:14:47,534
(The stone tower is finally complete.)

2019
01:14:47,559 --> 01:14:48,690
Now, let's pray.

2020
01:14:48,856 --> 01:14:49,724
Let's pray.

2021
01:14:49,725 --> 01:14:51,893
(Even the dog joins them.)

2022
01:14:52,194 --> 01:14:53,528
Please make us a huge success.

2023
01:14:53,770 --> 01:14:55,897
Please make Abra-ca-Empty a huge success.

2024
01:14:55,898 --> 01:14:56,765
A huge success.

2025
01:14:56,853 --> 01:14:59,086
- Make it a massive hit,
- A huge success.

2026
01:14:59,087 --> 01:15:01,770
so we can all become rich.

2027
01:15:01,795 --> 01:15:04,373
(A slightly greedy wish)

2028
01:15:05,306 --> 01:15:06,908
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2029
01:15:09,071 --> 01:15:15,104
(They even finish
with a little magic spell.)

2030
01:15:15,204 --> 01:15:19,382
- Make it come true!
- Come true!

2031
01:15:21,223 --> 01:15:23,154
(Perfectly in sync)

2032
01:15:25,706 --> 01:15:26,695
Is it this way?

2033
01:15:26,939 --> 01:15:28,281
(Four people, one wish.)

2034
01:15:28,306 --> 01:15:29,297
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

2035
01:15:29,599 --> 01:15:32,834
- Good.
- Wasn't the hike down pretty easy?

2036
01:15:32,835 --> 01:15:34,703
We walked down so far.

2037
01:15:34,704 --> 01:15:35,604
Did we?

2038
01:15:35,605 --> 01:15:37,139
So we have to go back up
and then head down.

2039
01:15:38,065 --> 01:15:39,152
(But then...)

2040
01:15:39,153 --> 01:15:41,343
No way!

2041
01:15:44,045 --> 01:15:48,910
(A torrential downpour begins
just as they start descending.)

2042
01:15:49,798 --> 01:15:51,885
- I think I'd like it if it rains.
- Me too.

2043
01:15:51,886 --> 01:15:53,622
Sorry to the staff, but...

2044
01:15:53,647 --> 01:15:56,425
(The sky grants
a completely different wish.)

2045
01:15:56,799 --> 01:15:57,759
What do we do?

2046
01:16:00,562 --> 01:16:02,130
What's with this rain?

2047
01:16:06,090 --> 01:16:07,736
I'm thirsty.

2048
01:16:07,924 --> 01:16:13,442
<i>Something has gone seriously wrong</i>

2049
01:16:14,543 --> 01:16:15,911
I can't believe this.

2050
01:16:15,936 --> 01:16:20,304
(Since it rained the entire way down,)

2051
01:16:20,329 --> 01:16:21,283
You're pretty.

2052
01:16:21,308 --> 01:16:25,946
(they seem to have lost their minds.)

2053
01:16:28,186 --> 01:16:31,252
(The one who enjoys
it is the true master.)

2054
01:16:31,452 --> 01:16:32,727
What's with her?

2055
01:16:35,127 --> 01:16:37,032
We're on a whole new level of crazy.

2056
01:16:37,180 --> 01:16:39,301
I'm so jealous of that silhouette.

2057
01:16:40,007 --> 01:16:41,001
I'm getting seahorse vibes.

2058
01:16:41,261 --> 01:16:43,405
I look like Hwang Jini.

2059
01:16:45,408 --> 01:16:47,275
You really look like Hwang Jini.

2060
01:16:48,376 --> 01:16:50,376
She finally found the perfect fit.

2061
01:16:50,612 --> 01:16:54,349
<i>Hwang Jini</i>

2062
01:16:54,988 --> 01:16:57,542
(And what's this person doing now?)

2063
01:16:57,642 --> 01:16:59,121
The dog came back down too.

2064
01:16:59,988 --> 01:17:02,390
Come on here.

2065
01:17:02,808 --> 01:17:04,025
I think it's coming to you.

2066
01:17:06,962 --> 01:17:08,396
You came down too?

2067
01:17:08,997 --> 01:17:10,699
So cute.

2068
01:17:14,055 --> 01:17:18,073
How does it go from blazing sunshine
to pouring rain like this?

2069
01:17:18,074 --> 01:17:19,040
That's so fascinating.

2070
01:17:19,082 --> 01:17:20,375
They ran into that dog again.

2071
01:17:20,809 --> 01:17:22,113
Hi, Won Ji.

2072
01:17:25,647 --> 01:17:27,182
You guys are still full of energy.

2073
01:17:27,582 --> 01:17:29,651
Let's go get something cold to drink.

2074
01:17:29,951 --> 01:17:32,087
- Let's go.
- I want some juice.

2075
01:17:32,128 --> 01:17:34,723
It was so hot, but getting rained on
actually cooled me down.

2076
01:17:34,724 --> 01:17:36,491
That was so nice.

2077
01:17:36,528 --> 01:17:37,626
I think this is the place.

2078
01:17:40,362 --> 01:17:41,963
We're here.

2079
01:17:43,040 --> 01:17:45,454
(A beach restaurant)

2080
01:17:46,675 --> 01:17:48,336
Everything looks delicious.

2081
01:17:48,937 --> 01:17:51,506
- The menu.
- I want a smoothie.

2082
01:17:52,207 --> 01:17:53,408
This is crazy.

2083
01:17:53,638 --> 01:17:54,609
What should we get?

2084
01:17:55,277 --> 01:17:59,473
(Everyone orders whatever they want.)

2085
01:17:59,498 --> 01:18:02,450
It's going to taste so good
when I get the first sip.

2086
01:18:02,498 --> 01:18:04,352
I feel like I could finish it in one gulp.

2087
01:18:04,749 --> 01:18:06,749
When our drinks arrive,
we should film that trend.

2088
01:18:08,409 --> 01:18:09,129
Ta-da.

2089
01:18:09,196 --> 01:18:10,592
Here's how it works.

2090
01:18:11,529 --> 01:18:12,943
(Playing)

2091
01:18:15,589 --> 01:18:18,707
(The Summoning Jutsu challenge
that's viral right now)

2092
01:18:19,381 --> 01:18:21,136
We just film one person at a time?

2093
01:18:21,570 --> 01:18:23,805
(She immediately gives it a try.)

2094
01:18:23,934 --> 01:18:26,741
You pause the recording, place the item,
then start recording again.

2095
01:18:26,787 --> 01:18:27,609
I'll go...

2096
01:18:28,143 --> 01:18:29,774
(The oldest is a little worried.)

2097
01:18:31,479 --> 01:18:32,681
Direct us.

2098
01:18:32,801 --> 01:18:33,981
(Don't worry.)

2099
01:18:34,302 --> 01:18:35,301
Drinks are here.

2100
01:18:35,354 --> 01:18:37,586
This is so fast.

2101
01:18:37,622 --> 01:18:39,696
(Sian's mango dragon fruit smoothie)

2102
01:18:39,721 --> 01:18:41,389
You should go first, Sian.

2103
01:18:41,823 --> 01:18:42,857
Just like this?

2104
01:18:42,970 --> 01:18:43,718
Very good.

2105
01:18:44,092 --> 01:18:45,756
(They even match the count.)

2106
01:18:47,663 --> 01:18:49,731
When you stop, I'll hand you the drink.

2107
01:18:52,901 --> 01:18:54,536
Let's do one more take, just in case.

2108
01:18:56,170 --> 01:18:57,672
You're good at this.

2109
01:18:57,673 --> 01:18:59,437
(Gabee immediately hands over the drink.)

2110
01:19:02,210 --> 01:19:03,457
(Laughing)

2111
01:19:03,458 --> 01:19:04,312
Again.

2112
01:19:09,104 --> 01:19:10,385
Well done.

2113
01:19:10,819 --> 01:19:12,591
I'll do...

2114
01:19:12,592 --> 01:19:13,755
How about this?

2115
01:19:13,756 --> 01:19:15,924
(The director enthusiastically
pitches an idea.)

2116
01:19:17,252 --> 01:19:19,332
(The choreography
comes together in no time.)

2117
01:19:19,333 --> 01:19:20,395
Looks nice.

2118
01:19:21,005 --> 01:19:21,852
(They start filming.)

2119
01:19:24,045 --> 01:19:25,500
Great.

2120
01:19:25,898 --> 01:19:27,439
(Amazed)

2121
01:19:29,099 --> 01:19:31,264
- She's on another level.
- Absolutely.

2122
01:19:31,792 --> 01:19:33,808
(So professional)

2123
